      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Implementing Delete Confirmation**\n\nI'm currently focused on adding a confirmation modal for topic deletion within the `Disciplinas` component. It's similar to the existing discipline deletion flow, ensuring a consistent user experience. I aim to replicate the modal behavior for topic removal, so accidental deletions are minimized, and data loss is avoided.\n\n\n**Refining Edit Implementation**\n\nI'm now diving into the `Disciplinas.tsx` component, adding states for deletion confirmation and editing. Specifically, I'm setting up states for `topicToDelete`, `editingSubjectId`, `editingTopicId`, and `editValue` to facilitate both actions. I'm focusing on inline editing for a cleaner UI, and I'm updating `removeTopic` logic for confirmation. I'm also preparing `updateSubjectName` and `updateTopicTitle` functions. I've started planning the required state changes within the component.\n\n\n**Implementing Edit Workflow**\n\nI'm now implementing the edit functionality, focusing on inline editing within the `Disciplinas` component. I'm adding states to manage `editingSubjectId`, `editingTopicId`, and `editValue`. I'm also planning to utilize `Edit3`, `Check`, and `X` icons from `lucide-react` for a cleaner UI. I'll replace text with inputs conditionally, and will implement `saveSubjectName`, `handleEditTopic`, and `saveTopicTitle` to manage state updates effectively, with save/cancel controls.\n\n\n",
