      "text": "**Reviewing Existing Code**\n\nOkay, I'm diving into the `Disciplinas` component code. I see that name editing is partially implemented for subject names and topic titles, based on the previous turn's work. I'm focusing on adding the specific subject name edit functionality, which seems to have been left incomplete.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Details**\n\nIt seems the subject name editing functionality is partially there in the `Disciplinas` component, including state management and conditional rendering for an input field. My task now seems to be refining it. I'm considering if the user might want a more obvious implementation. I will check the code content from the prompt to see how this can be improved.\n\n\n**Considering UX Improvements**\n\nI've examined the provided code snippet, focusing on the inline editing of subject names within the `Disciplinas` component. The core functionality seems present, including the handling of input, saving changes on Enter, and cancelling. I'm now contemplating UX enhancements, specifically around the \"Edit\" trigger. The current hover-based icon is functional, but perhaps a more explicit \"Edit\" button for increased clarity and user-friendliness would be better. I noted the use of `e as any` in `onKeyDown` and will confirm whether that is needed or not.\n\n\n**Verifying Complete Functionality**\n\nI've re-examined the code. The user's requests, including confirmation modals for topic removal and editing for subject/topic names, are present. Perhaps they missed the hover effect on the \"Edit3\" icon. I'll focus on improving visibility of the edit functionality, potentially by adding an explicit \"Rename\" option in the dropdown. I will also check to ensure the \"Edit Subject\" and \"Edit Topic\" functionality is sound.\n\n\n**Enhancing Edit Functionality**\n\nI'm revisiting the `Disciplinas.tsx` file, focusing on refining the edit functionality. The code already has logic for subject and topic name editing, along with `e.stopPropagation()`. I'm verifying the \"Edit\" icons' discoverability and the smoothness of the interactions. I'm also adding a small indicator for the AI cycle's importance/Pareto principles. I will update `Disciplinas.tsx` to include these improvements. I'll focus on polishing the interaction flows.\n\n\n**Confirming Core Features**\n\nI'm confirming the existing implementation of subject and topic deletion modals, along with the editing state management for both subjects and topics, is functional. I've re-examined the code in `Disciplinas.tsx` to verify these parts exist, and it appears they are already implemented. I'm focusing on user experience, specifically making the edit functionality more obvious. I'll make the edit button always visible on the subject name.\n\n\n",
