    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Improving Button Visibility**\n\nOkay, I'm focusing on the edit and delete buttons in the `Disciplinas` component. The current design makes them too difficult to find. I'm exploring increased opacity and visual styling – maybe subtle icons or different colors for improved recognition. Right now, I'm leaning toward subtle visual cues to highlight them without being overly intrusive to the user interface.\n\n\n**Refining Button Visibility Strategy**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a new strategy, aiming for permanent button visibility, albeit subtly dimmed initially. The current `opacity-0` approach causes confusion on mobile, as expected. I'm considering enhancing button recognition via contrasting colors and layout improvements to minimize visual clutter. A dedicated \"Actions\" menu is also on the table, alongside a layout that accommodates these improvements without appearing cluttered, with mobile compatibility as a core priority. The `Disciplinas` component is the location I'm updating.\n\n\n**Implementing Subtle Enhancements**\n\nI'm now implementing the changes to improve button visibility, moving away from `opacity-0` altogether. I'm opting for a base opacity or standard `text-slate-400` to ensure they're always visible. I'm adding rounded backgrounds and setting specific colors for the icons: `text-indigo-400` for the edit icon and `text-rose-400` for the delete icon. I'm also including hover effects like `hover:bg-indigo-50` and `hover:bg-rose-50` for added visual feedback, focusing on the `Disciplinas` component.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769108171,
      "nanos": 340000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
