    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Defining Review Functionality**\n\nI'm now focusing on defining the specifics for the review functionality. I'm prioritizing listing all completed topics across subjects. Also, I need to configure the review due dates, specifically 7, 15, and 30 days post-completion (`lastStudiedAt`). I need to include a \"complete review\" button and fields for recording the number of questions attempted.\n\n\n**Analyzing Review Data Display**\n\nI'm now considering how best to present review data. I need to display the \"questions correct,\" \"hit rate,\" and \"time spent,\" likely mirroring the topic stats on the \"Disciplinas\" page. I'm taking a look at `components/Revisao.tsx`, and how it currently filters topics by due date using `diffDays`. It seems the user wants a comprehensive view of all completed topics and their upcoming 7, 15, and 30-day review dates, possibly as pending reviews.\n\n\n**Refining Review Stats**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on review session statistics. It seems crucial to log data *specifically* for each review (7, 15, and 30-day). The `Topic` type seems insufficient for this, as its fields are likely for aggregate or last session data. The user's feedback, \"cadastro semelhante ao do cadastro de tópicos,\" leans towards updating the existing fields, but I'm considering adding specific fields, or perhaps storing specific review data. I need to figure out how to best integrate session data, and the existing `Disciplinas.tsx` editing panel might be the key to replicating this within `Revisao.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Review Details**\n\nI'm now implementing the review details on each topic, mirroring the editing panel from \"Disciplinas\". The \"Concluir Revisão\" button will save review stats, potentially updating existing fields, but not the `lastStudiedAt` date, to maintain the original completion date for review scheduling. Also, I've confirmed that the \"Timezone Fix\" needs to be implemented here as well. I'm now certain the 7, 15, and 30-day deadlines are *fixed* from initial completion, and not reset by a review.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
