    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Revision Mechanics**\n\nI'm currently focused on the \"Revisão\" page and its existing functionality. My understanding is that the current system registers revisions, which then triggers an update of the `lastStudiedAt` parameter, which results in the resetting of the study cycle. The request clarifies that revisions shouldn't be postponed. I need to understand how the system manages the study cycles in order to implement this constraint.\n\n\n**Refining Revision Tracking**\n\nI've decided to track revision milestones using a `revisionsDone: number[]` array within the `Topic` type, storing completed days (7, 15, 30). This allows for separate \"check-off\" functionality in the UI, enabling users to monitor their milestone completion, with dates, independent of when they revise. The plan is to base the 7/15/30 day cycle on the initial completion date and show completed milestones. I am reviewing the data model now.\n\n\n**Implementing Revision Marking**\n\nNow I'm focusing on the UI for marking revisions as completed in `Revisao.tsx`. I'll add checkboxes next to \"7 Days,\" \"15 Days,\" and \"30 Days.\" The data model in `Topic` will be updated to include `revisionsDone?: number[]`. The milestone dates will be calculated based on the `lastStudiedAt` value. The registration of stats is now planned to aggregate the stats, and I'll revisit the \"Registrar Revisão\" button, which opens a panel. When a user saves, they will indicate which revision milestone they're completing by checking the corresponding box.\n\n\n**Defining Milestone Functionality**\n\nI'm now refining the UI for the \"Revisao.tsx\" page. I'm adding buttons for the 7, 15, and 30-day milestones on each card. When \"Registrar Revisão\" is clicked, I'll allow inputting stats and selecting the completed milestones. Crucially, `lastStudiedAt` won't change upon marking a revision, unless the user explicitly wants to reset the cycle. Fixed intervals from the original completion date are the goal. I am updating my plans for aggregating stats and possibly storing revision history.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
