    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Developing Study Counter**\n\nI'm currently focused on integrating a \"Study Hours Counter\" into the \"Dashboard.\" This involves aggregating study time from both \"Disciplinas\" and \"Revisões\" pages. I'm also planning to implement a \"Weekly Study Goal\" feature, allowing customization of the target study hours.\n\n\n**Implementing Weekly Reset Logic**\n\nI've been working on the weekly reset logic for the study progress. I realized the existing `studyTimeMinutes` in `Topic` is cumulative, presenting a challenge for a weekly goal reset. Therefore, I'm refactoring the implementation in `App.tsx` and related types. I'm focusing on calculating weekly study time. I'll need to figure out how to best integrate the existing `studyTimeMinutes` from `Disciplinas` and `Revisao` for the comparison, without requiring a complete session history log.\n\n\n**Refining Study Tracking**\n\nI'm now refining the study tracking mechanism. My initial approach of adding a `studyHistory` field seems overly complex. I've opted for a simpler solution: adding a `weeklyGoal` to the user or global state and using a `studyLog` to track individual sessions. I'm focusing on defining the `StudySession` interface in `types.ts` and managing the `weeklyGoal` and `studyLogs` in `App.tsx`. The goal is to calculate total study hours and \"this week\" hours in the dashboard, and display the weekly goal progress. I'm updating `Disciplinas.tsx` and `Revisao.tsx` to save `StudyLog` entries upon saving study stats.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769110921,
      "nanos": 2000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769110930,
