  {
    "id": 59,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Designing Dark Mode**\n\nI'm currently focused on designing a dark mode for the app, covering every page: Dashboard, Disciplinas, Ciclos, Revisão, Simulados, and Login. The goal is to establish two fully functional, visually appealing environments – light and dark. I need to figure out the right state management approach for the theme.\n\n\n**Implementing the Theme Toggle**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the mechanics of the light/dark toggle. Specifically, I need to integrate the button, leverage Tailwind's `dark:` classes, and consider how the `index.html` file should be updated, although I think it is best managed as a state-driven class on a wrapper. Furthermore, I need to update all key components. I'm focusing on the component adaptation for dark mode, like backgrounds. For example, I'm thinking `bg-slate-50` for light and `bg-slate-950` for dark.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769111973,
      "nanos": 450000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769111979,
      "nanos": 627000000
    }
