    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering Light Mode Implementation**\n\nI'm currently focused on incorporating a light mode option for the application. The foundation is there, with `isDarkMode` state, a toggle button, and persistence in `localStorage`. The next step is to make sure the app works with light mode in mind.\n\n\n**Assessing Toggle Visibility**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the light/dark mode toggle visibility. Examining the `App.tsx` component, the logic appears sound, correctly using the `isDarkMode` state. However, the user's request suggests the implementation isn't immediately obvious. The current styling and placement of the toggle might need refinement to improve its prominence and make the feature easily discoverable. I think more user feedback is needed.\n\n\n**Refining Theme Switcher Prominence**\n\nI'm now focusing on making the light/dark mode switch more prominent and user-friendly. Reviewing previous implementations, I realized the switch is already implemented, but users might miss it. So, I will refine the `App.tsx` sidebar to improve the switch's visibility, ensuring every component has high-quality \"light mode\" aesthetics. I'm also reviewing `index.html` to prevent any forced mode defaults and ensuring color harmony across both modes.\n\n\n**Optimizing User Interface**\n\nI'm now implementing a dedicated \"Theme Switcher\" section in the sidebar with a premium feel, such as a segmented control, and I'll audit all components for color contrast and visual balance in light mode. Charts and complex UI elements will be refined for high-quality visuals in both environments. Light mode will use soft slates, vibrant indigo accents, and subtle shadows; Dark mode will use deep navy/slate tones, neon-ish indigo glows and border-based separation. I'll also refine `App.tsx` for theme toggle visibility and add it to the mobile top bar.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
