      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Troubleshooting Display Mode**\n\nI'm now investigating a persistent issue: the website stubbornly stays in dark mode, even when \"light mode\" is selected. My focus is the `App.tsx` file, specifically the state management related to `isDarkMode`. I'm checking the `localStorage` interactions to see if the saved preference is overriding the user's choice.\n\n\n**Analyzing Theme Logic**\n\nI've examined the Tailwind implementation, and the `App.tsx` logic appears sound for managing dark mode state using `localStorage` and system preferences. My attention has shifted to the base styling. The `index.html` has a light mode default. Now, I'm verifying the application of the `dark:` prefix consistently across all components, focusing on background colors. The root cause must be identified in a component that hasn't switched.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Style Inconsistencies**\n\nI've been scrutinizing the `className` attributes for `bg-` styles and `dark:` prefixes. Initial observations suggested consistent application, but the theme switcher buttons in `App.tsx` may contain inconsistencies. I am reviewing the logic within the `className` attributes that are being conditionally applied based on `isDarkMode`. The current focus is the visual application of state, which determines light vs dark.\n\n\n**Examining Color Application**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the button styles in `App.tsx`, and I'm seeing an inconsistency. Both theme buttons have the same background colors, regardless of selection. I'm focusing on the `className` attributes and conditional logic to identify how the `isDarkMode` state is applied. My attention is now on the `index.html` file and its body class to ensure theme application is correct. I am examining if the application of the dark class is conflicting. I am reviewing background color application across the site.\n\n\n**Investigating Background Colors**\n\nI'm now focusing on background colors. In light mode, the default should be `bg-slate-50`, and the `Dashboard` component seems to be correctly set to white (`bg-white`). The issue seems isolated. I'm focusing on why a light theme isn't applied. It might be in the global styles of the `index.html`, where the body's default class is `bg-slate-50`. I'm going to investigate what renders into `#root` and see why this isn't taking effect. I am also checking `App.tsx`'s `isDarkMode` state is set and applied correctly to the root div. I am going to check for other config files that might change things.\n\n\n**Confirming Theme Configuration**\n\nI'm now implementing the `tailwind.config = { darkMode: 'class' }` configuration within `index.html` to override the default media query strategy. I'm ensuring all components have their intended light mode classes, which has helped clarify the theme configuration. My primary focus is verifying that the theme toggle buttons in `App.tsx` correctly reflect the current state and are properly triggering the class-based dark mode switch. I've noted that the site is, unexpectedly, all in dark mode; this behavior strongly suggests a media-based configuration, making the `class` strategy a crucial fix. I'm focusing on validating the conditional application of light mode styles.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
