  {
    "id": 78,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Expanding Topic Input**\n\nI'm currently working on expanding the topic input functionality. The main focus now is enabling users to add multiple topics simultaneously. I'm taking into account the need for a unique numbering system preceding each topic to distinguish multiple entries, especially nested ones such as \"1.1\".\n\n\n**Refining Bulk Input**\n\nI'm now refining the bulk input method for topics. I've shifted from a single-line input to a textarea, which is a more flexible approach. A parser is being implemented that should recognize topic numbering patterns, like \"1.2.3 Calculus.\" Initially, a regex `(\\d+(\\.\\d+)*)\\s*(.*)` was drafted, but simple line-splitting by number may be adequate. The new \"Bulk Add\" modal will offer a clean UI. The visuals will include a text area for syllabus content. I am currently working on implementing the new states.\n\n\n**Parsing Topic Inputs**\n\nI've been working on parsing the bulk topic input. I'm focusing on splitting the input by newline and then parsing each line. I'm using a regular expression, `^([\\d.]+)\\s*(.*)`, to extract the numbering and title, then store them separately. I'm considering keeping the numbering as part of the title for now. I'm going to test the parsing thoroughly for different input formats.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769112923,
      "nanos": 289000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
