    "id": 86,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering User Management Features**\n\nI'm currently focused on incorporating user management. I'm thinking about the essentials: registration, profile editing, account deletion, and password changes. The existing login component and session management are a starting point. Now, I need to design the best strategy for each user management feature.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the practical steps. I'm focusing on the component-level changes needed. First I will handle updating the types, then modifying the application to accommodate the different scenarios for user creation and deletion. I will enhance the login component for signup and creating the self-service profile component. Lastly, I will update the admin dashboard.\n\n\n**Implementing User Management Actions**\n\nI've outlined specific component changes. I'll add a \"Sign Up\" toggle to `Login.tsx`, and a `Profile` state/modal in `App.tsx`. A new `Profile.tsx` component handles profile and password edits. I will modify `Admin.tsx` to include user management. I'll also add a \"Forgot Password\" mock, and make sure that `global_users` is updated when users sign up, log in, edit their profiles, or delete their profiles. I will start by modifying `Login.tsx`.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
