    "id": 93,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering User Management**\n\nI'm focusing on the admin User Management page. My goal is to revamp the \"Status\" column to display \"ativo/bloqueado\" instead of \"active/inactive.\" I've also incorporated the user's desire to add an \"Online\" column for user real-time status visibility.\n\n\n**Refining User State Logic**\n\nI'm now diving deeper into how to represent user \"online\" status within the conceptual app. Given the constraints of using `localStorage`, I'm evaluating a few approaches. Checking `lastAccess` seems feasible, but I'm leaning toward a simpler `isOnline` boolean, potentially derived from the existing status. I need to make sure the \"blocked\" status is properly reflected and I have a clear plan for both \"online\" and \"blocked\" status. The request specifically asks for status (active/blocked) and a separate \"online\" column. I need to either add `isBlocked` to the `User` type or repurpose `status`.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Status Definition**\n\nI've made progress in clarifying the `User` status and online representation. The `status` field in the `User` interface will be changed to reflect \"ativo\" or \"bloqueado,\" corresponding to account enablement. In addition to this, a separate `isOnline` boolean will manage user real-time presence. I am updating `Admin.tsx` to reflect the status changes. I'll translate the table headers to Aluno, Acesso, Status. The goal is to reflect status and online presence. `App.tsx` has been slated for login/logout updates.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
