    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Adding Edit Functionality**\n\nI'm focusing on incorporating an edit feature into the Admin component. My immediate goal is to implement an \"edit\" button alongside the existing create and delete actions, which will trigger a modal form for modifying existing editais. I'm prioritizing building the UI, specifically the edit modal, and its date fields, next.\n\n\n**Addressing Date Discrepancy**\n\nI've encountered a timezone bug with date handling, where exam dates are off by a day. I'm modifying the `Admin.tsx` to directly store the date string from the input, thus avoiding the `new Date()` timezone pitfalls. Additionally, when displaying the dates, I'm refraining from directly using `new Date()` and applying formatting directly to the input string. The \"edit\" functionality has been implemented, and an `editingEdital` state, along with the `openEditEdital(edital)` function, and a separate button to select an edital for editing, are all implemented in order to ensure editing functions.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
