ow verifying data storage within the registration flow. I've updated the `onLogin` function to ensure new user data, including the initial role, is correctly persisted in local storage. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity when new users are created and how existing error cases are handled. I've verified that the new `global_users` data is correctly created.\n\n\n**Refining Form Validation**\n\nI'm now revising the registration form's validation. I've integrated checks for empty fields and password matching, which is working. I'm currently verifying the email uniqueness check against the existing user list in local storage. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency and implementing clear error messages.\n\n\n**Validating Registration Logic**\n\nI'm now implementing form validation within `Login.tsx`. I've added error messages and handling. I am checking the `handleRegister` and related functions. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency and providing helpful error feedback. The next step is validating the email uniqueness with a new helper function. I will be checking to see if there is an existing user.\n\n\n**Implementing Email Validation**\n\nI'm now implementing the email uniqueness check during registration within the `Login.tsx` component. I'm building a dedicated helper function to iterate through existing user data in local storage and verify the email address is not already in use. I am making sure the error state is accurately updated to reflect the new validation rule.\n\n```\n<div className=\"relative group\">\n  <Lock className=\"absolute left-4 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-slate-400 group-focus-within:text-indigo-600 transition-colors\" size={18} />\n    <input\n    type=\"password\"\n    required\n    className=\"w-full pl-12 pr-4 py-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-white outline-none font-bold\"\n    placeholder=\"Sua Senha\"\n    value={passwor