    "id": 143,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Login Failure Scenarios**\n\nI'm currently focused on implementing a \"Blocked User\" warning system for login failures. The goal is to alert users after multiple unsuccessful attempts, specifically after the 5th failure. A warning, \"Only 2 more attempts left\" will be provided on the 3rd failed attempt. I'm also ensuring the admin account remains exempt from this blocking mechanism. I'm looking into updating `Login.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining Login Flow Updates**\n\nI'm now integrating the failure counter into the login process, primarily in `Login.tsx`. I'm using `localStorage` to track failed attempts per email address. For admins, I'm ensuring they bypass the blocking mechanism but still receive the warning messages. The `handleSubmit` function in `Login.tsx` is being updated to manage the different warning levels for failures. I've also incorporated the specific failure messages, including the blocking notice for non-admins, and updating the user's status to 'blocked' in global storage upon the 5th failed attempt.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769118693,
      "nanos": 5000000
    },
