    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Data Loss Issue**\n\nI'm focused on the data loss problem during application updates, suspecting the state management within `App.tsx` is the culprit. I'm considering initialization and saving methods. Also, I'm thinking about adding performance tracking, specifically around hours spent, questions attempted, and the number of questions answered correctly per topic. I need to make sure the user data is properly persisted.\n\n\n**Implementing Performance Tracking**\n\nI'm now incorporating performance tracking UI elements within `Disciplinas.tsx` to display study time, questions attempted, and correct answers per topic. I'm focusing on ensuring data persistence in `App.tsx` and preventing initial state issues that could overwrite `localStorage` data. I'm also reviewing `types.ts` to confirm the presence of needed fields in the `Topic` type. I'm working on adding a form to track inputs and display a hit rate indicator.\n\n\n**Refining Data Persistence Logic**\n\nI'm tackling the \"users are lost\" issue. The core is that `allUsers` can be initially an empty array, which triggers undesired behavior when the save effect runs before the load effect. I'm focusing on ensuring data persistence in `App.tsx` by using an `isLoaded` flag to prevent saving before loading. I'll also double-check `@google/genai` usage in `geminiService.ts` against the coding guidelines, confirming imports, initialization, model choice, and response property access, along with the `Type` enum in the schema.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI for Performance**\n\nI'm now implementing the UI updates in `Disciplinas.tsx` for performance tracking. I'm focusing on the input fields for hours, minutes, questions attempted, and correct answers per topic within the expanded topic list. I'll add a \"Confirm\" button to trigger `onAddLog` and update the `subjects` state. I'll also calculate and display a percentage. I'm using icons for the performance trigger and color-coded badges to indicate performance levels. I also added a check to `App.tsx` ensuring it returns early from the save effect if `isLoaded` is false.\n\n\n**Verifying Loading Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on ensuring that the `isLoaded` flag in `App.tsx` is initialized to `false` and only set to `true` after the loading effect completes, preventing premature data saving. I'm also refining the UI in `Disciplinas.tsx` to include an expanded \"Log Performance\" tray with input fields for hours, minutes, questions attempted, and correct answers per topic. This is in addition to existing stats. I'll also double-check for potential race conditions and ensure `geminiService.ts` follows coding guidelines.\n\n\n",
