      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering Database Integration**\n\nI'm currently focused on integrating a Supabase database into my React application. The key files I'm working with are `index.tsx`, which serves as the entry point, `App.tsx`, where I'm managing the main logic and state (using `localStorage` at the moment), and `services/geminiService.ts`, which contains the AI logic. The goal is to migrate from `localStorage` to Supabase for data persistence and scalability.\n\n\n**Refining Supabase Implementation**\n\nI'm now diving deeper into the required database schema, specifically the `users`, `subjects`, `topics`, `study_logs`, `study_cycles`, `mock_exams`, and `predefined_editais` tables. I'm focusing on the necessary CRUD operations and how to sync my React state with Supabase, replacing the current `localStorage` usage. I will also be removing `index.html` to improve the project structure. I'm preparing to initialize the Supabase client and handle authentication (sign-up/login) as a priority. I also need to make sure I add `@supabase/supabase-js` as a dependency, and the respective environment variables.\n\n\n**Addressing Bundling Issues**\n\nI've resolved the Rollup error regarding `@google/generative-ai` by clarifying the Vite project's reliance on `package.json` for bundling. I'm cleaning up `index.html` by removing the redundant `importmap` and confirming the presence of necessary libraries in `package.json`. My next steps involve initializing the Supabase client in `lib/supabase.ts`, refactoring `App.tsx` to utilize Supabase for state and effects, and ensuring the `types.ts` file reflects the database schema. Since I will not be using the actual Supabase credentials for this exercise, I'll assume their availability via `process.env`.\n\n\n**Implementing Relational Database**\n\nI'm now revising the database schema to use UUIDs for IDs, facilitating relational structure. The `Login` component will leverage Supabase Auth. Upon login, I need to fetch the user's specific data, with an admin view fetching all users and editais. I will focus on integrating `@supabase/supabase-js`, initializing the client in `lib/supabase.ts`, and overhauling `App.tsx`'s logic. I'm removing the `importmap` from `index.html` to resolve build errors and making sure `@google/generative-ai` is properly resolved. New tables will include `profiles`, `subjects`, and `topics`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Implementation Steps**\n\nI'm now nailing down the precise steps for Supabase integration. I'll update `package.json` to include `@supabase/supabase-js` and make sure `vite.config.ts` includes the necessary environment variables. The main focus will be updating `App.tsx` for Supabase authentication and data handling. Given the environment setup, I'll leverage `process.env` for API keys and Supabase credentials. A `supabaseService.ts` will encapsulate all Supabase interactions, assuming database schema is already set, or with guidance in comments.\n\n\n",
