      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Supabase Initialization**\n\nI'm focusing on the \"supabaseUrl is required\" error. It seems `supabaseUrl` and `supabaseAnonKey` are undefined when `createClient` runs in `lib/supabase.ts`. I'm examining `vite.config.ts`, where environment variables are defined, trying to trace why the variables aren't being set properly. I'm hoping to identify the source of the empty values.\n\n\n**Investigating Environment Variables**\n\nI've zeroed in on the `vite.config.ts` file and noticed environment variables are being stringified, with fallback to empty strings. This confirms the problem: `SUPABASE_URL` is likely undefined at build time, resulting in an empty string. The `supabase-js` library rightly throws if no URL exists. My next step is implementing checks for variable presence before `createClient` and considering fallbacks. I am going to see if I can allow the app to boot even with no Supabase.\n\n\n**Refining Variable Handling**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a robust solution for managing missing Supabase keys. My revised strategy involves checking for the presence of `supabaseUrl` and `supabaseAnonKey` before calling `createClient`. If either is missing, I will log a clear error message, and export a mock client, potentially `null`. This will prevent the app from crashing and allow a graceful fallback. The goal is to provide a good user experience while still allowing a functional app even without Supabase. I am trying to use Vite's `define` property to pass the necessary values down.\n\n\n**Addressing Missing Credentials**\n\nI've determined that the root cause of the Supabase error lies in missing or empty environment variables. I'm focusing on `lib/supabase.ts` and realized that the credentials are evaluating to empty strings, which is expected behaviour. I am updating `lib/supabase.ts` to handle missing credentials gracefully by conditionally calling `createClient`. Simultaneously, I'll remove the `importmap` from `index.html`, which seems to be adding to the resolution issues. I'm double-checking consistent `process.env` access.\n\n\n",
