      "text": "To resolve the `Uncaught Error: supabaseUrl is required.` error, we need to prevent the Supabase client from initializing if the environment variables are missing. We will also update the `App.tsx` to handle cases where the database is not configured, ensuring the application remains functional (perhaps falling back to local storage or showing a warning) instead of crashing on boot.\n\n### Specification:\n1.  **`lib/supabase.ts`**: Update the initialization logic. We will only call `createClient` if both the URL and Key are provided. If missing, we export `null` to prevent the hard crash.\n2.  **`App.tsx`**: Add defensive checks around all Supabase calls. If `supabase` is `null`, the app will skip database synchronization and operate in a \"local-only\" mode or show a clear initialization warning.\n3.  **`index.html`**: Remove the `importmap` block. As seen in the logs, this causes conflicts with Vite's build process and can lead to unexpected resolution errors in production.\n4.  **`components/Login.tsx`**: Add a check to prevent submission if the database is not configured.\n\n---\n\n",
