    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing Login Modifications**\n\nI see the user confirmed the core functionality works, but now they're having trouble logging in, likely due to recent code changes. I'm focusing on the `App.tsx` file and examining the authentication logic, specifically the usage of `supabase.auth.getSession()` and the `supabase` client itself. It looks like the login flow may be modified, so I'm investigating how the changes affect the authentication process.\n\n\n**Analyzing Authentication Flow**\n\nI've examined the authentication flow, specifically how `Login.tsx` uses `supabase.auth.signUp()` and `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()`. I've verified `lib/supabase.ts` is correctly initialized. I realized the user may have set the Supabase URL and Key in Vercel incorrectly. So, I added logic to swap them, which might resolve the login issue. However, they are still having issues logging in, which usually means they are on the login screen and can't get past it. I'm considering email confirmation issues and a missing `profiles` table as potential causes.\n\n\n**Refining User Profile Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on how the `user` state is managed in `App.tsx`. Specifically, I'm concerned if the `profiles` table is empty or the trigger failed. If the `profile` isn't found, the `setUser` state won't update, keeping the user stuck on the login page even with a valid session. I'm modifying `Login.tsx` and `App.tsx` to handle this scenario gracefully, ensuring a basic profile is created, even if temporarily, for a smoother \"Welcome\" experience. The recent \"modified\" comment makes me think these fallback values are the core of the problem.\n\n\n**Clarifying Account Creation**\n\nI'm now focusing on the initial account creation flow. It's likely the user needs to register before logging in, especially with a new database. I'm modifying `App.tsx` to handle missing profiles by creating a default user object to prevent the login hang. I'll also add a clearer registration message in `Login.tsx` to guide users to the \"Sign Up\" option, as they are likely looking for the login credentials when they first load. Finally, I'll provide improved feedback on account registration to ease that flow.\n\n\n**Improving Data Fetching**\n\nI'm now revising how `App.tsx` handles profile data retrieval. If the initial table lookup fails, I'll leverage data from the authentication metadata to avoid getting stuck on the login screen. I'm focusing on improved error messages within the login form for better visual clarity. I've updated the logic in `App.tsx` so that `setUser` is always called, even with fallback values from `session.user`.\n\n\n**Enhancing Session Handling**\n\nI'm now implementing more robust session handling. I'm leveraging user metadata for immediate app access post-signup. Specifically, if the database lookup fails in `App.tsx`, I'll use the user's `session.user` data to initialize a basic profile, ensuring a smoother login flow. Also, I've confirmed that the logic in `lib/supabase.ts` correctly handles the Vercel Supabase URL issue. I've updated `Login.tsx` to clearly differentiate login from registration with a prominent \"Cadastre-se\" link, so new users will be directed to register. I am now providing the most recent implementation.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
