      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Troubleshooting Email Issues**\n\nI'm currently investigating a problem with email confirmation within the Supabase authentication flow. The user isn't receiving the expected confirmation emails after signing up. I'm focusing on the typical Supabase behavior of sending these emails upon signup to ensure user verification. I'll need to assess why this crucial step isn't functioning as designed.\n\n\n**Addressing Email Confirmation Challenges**\n\nI've realized that a potential issue is the \"Confirm Email\" setting in Supabase. Because I can't access the Supabase dashboard to disable it, I need to update the `Login.tsx` component to handle this scenario effectively. Specifically, I will address the friction users experience if they can't confirm their email and incorporate a more informative error message. I'm focusing on providing clear instructions and potentially utilizing a feature of Supabase Auth to improve the user experience, given that I can't change the Supabase settings.\n\n\n**Refining Email Handling Logic**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the interaction between `Login.tsx` and the Supabase authentication flow. Specifically, I'm focusing on user-facing errors related to unconfirmed emails. I'm going to enhance the `handleSubmit` function in `Login.tsx` to explicitly handle the `email_not_confirmed` error code from Supabase. I'll include a prominent visual cue and a \"resend confirmation\" option, if possible. I'll need to reference `App.tsx` too to ensure everything works smoothly.\n\n\n**Improving Email Error Handling**\n\nI'm now integrating a `resendConfirmation` function within `Login.tsx` to directly address email confirmation issues. I'll enhance the error messages in `Login.tsx` for the \"Email not confirmed\" error, providing explicit user guidance. I am also implementing a diagnostic check in `App.tsx` or `Login.tsx` to help the user identify if the email confirmation is required.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
