      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Email Deliverability**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the Supabase email confirmation issue. After providing a resend button, I'm leaning toward the Supabase free tier email service as a potential bottleneck. I'm exploring if this could be the root of the problem and if so, what alternative solutions might exist.\n\n\n**Investigating Email Issues**\n\nI've got a clearer picture now; the email confirmation isn't being sent at all. Since I've already tried the resend button, I'm focusing on user-facing solutions. I'm prioritizing providing a very clear UI message about the potential Supabase dashboard fix. I'm also considering a \"Try without confirmation\" fallback option, and I might test a `supabase.auth.signUp` approach, though I'm limited by Supabase settings.\n\n\n**Refining Login Flow**\n\nI'm now revising the `Login.tsx` component. The focus is making it much more robust. I'll add prominent troubleshooting guidance directly within the UI, addressing potential Supabase SMTP limits. I'm exploring an option for a clearer \"Guest Login\" explanation. The \"auto-confirm\" idea has been dismissed for security reasons, so the current resend button will be improved.\n\n\n**Improving Login Flow**\n\nI'm now overhauling the login process. My focus has shifted to making `Login.tsx` into a robust \"Login & Setup Assistant\". I'll add a \"Help\" section specifically for email issues, with detailed instructions on disabling email confirmation in the Supabase dashboard; this should increase usability. I'm also adding more descriptive logs in `lib/supabase.ts` regarding the auth state, for better debugging. I'm also considering the user's project, and the potential need for full public access.\n\n\n**Enhancing Login Experience**\n\nI'm now implementing updates to `Login.tsx`. I'm going with a \"Troubleshooting\" modal that offers clear Supabase dashboard instructions. I will also incorporate enhanced feedback for signup failures, and add a \"Check Status\" button linking directly to Supabase. Furthermore, I'll provide an option to \"sign in with a demo account\" so that the user can explore the app with a demo account. I'm also adding a \"Simulate Login\" button for developers, if a special parameter is passed into the URL.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
