      "text": "**Integrating the Table**\n\nI've got the `subjects` table structure figured out, it's pretty straightforward. Now I'm focusing on the best way to integrate it with the TypeScript application. I'm thinking about how to efficiently fetch and manipulate the data, especially the JSONB `topics` column, within the codebase. What is the most efficient method to do so?\n\n\n**Adapting the Application**\n\nI'm adapting the application to interact with the new `subjects` table. I've updated the `types.ts` file to include `Subject` and `Topic` definitions, initialized the Supabase client in `lib/supabase.ts`, and I am now working on modifications to `App.tsx`. The existing logic assumed a `user_id` column, which doesn't exist in the user's provided SQL; Their table has just `id`, `name`, and `topics`. I'm updating `App.tsx` and `Disciplinas.tsx` to align with this new structure, including adjusting for the `bigint` vs. `string` type discrepancy for the `id` column. I need to insert code to use this new table.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Flow**\n\nI'm now implementing the data flow with the `subjects` table. I'm focusing on the component updates. First, `fetchUserData` in `App.tsx` has been updated to use the new table structure. Then, I added logic to sync changes to the database. Next, I'm working through updates to `Disciplinas.tsx`, including an `insert` in Supabase on `addSubject`, and an update on `addTopic`. I am handling the ID type mismatch between the database's `bigint` and the app's `string` by letting Supabase generate and return the ID on insert.\n\n\n**Revising CRUD Operations**\n\nI'm now revising the CRUD operations, focusing on `Disciplinas.tsx` and `App.tsx`. I need to fully integrate the Supabase client with these components, specifically addressing the table structure. I'm updating `addSubject`, `addTopic`, and `removeSubject` in `Disciplinas.tsx` and the subject fetching in `App.tsx`. I am also now handling the `bigint` vs `string` `id` issue by ensuring the TypeScript `Subject` interface can handle numeric DB IDs while keeping string IDs for the UI consistency. I want to keep the process simple, just update the components to use Supabase.\n\n\n",
