      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Button Behavior**\n\nI've pinpointed the malfunctioning \"Adicionar Disciplina\" button within `Disciplinas.tsx`. The code reveals the `addSubject` function, which leverages `supabase.from('subjects')`. Currently, my focus is on how this function is triggered and what data is being passed to it when the button is pressed. I'm checking for errors and ensuring the correct interaction between the button click event and the function call.\n\n\n**Investigating Insert Errors**\n\nI've discovered the root cause of the insertion failure: a `color` column is being sent to the database. The SQL table schema, as I've verified, does not include a `color` column. The `addSubject` function in the `Disciplinas.tsx` file is constructing an object to be inserted with this extraneous data. My next step is to remove this property. I am also checking the trigger and the data being sent.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI'm now implementing more robust error handling within the `addSubject` function to address the inconsistent database schema. The issue was that I introduced the `color` field, but it doesn't exist in the provided SQL. I will remove the `color` field from the insert operation to align with the database schema and add some more checks on whether the `user_id` is required. I'll also check the `types.ts` file to see what's happening there. I am logging any errors to the console, too.\n\n\n**Addressing Database Consistency**\n\nI'm now assessing the implications of the public access policy, and how that influences data consistency. I'm focusing on the `Disciplinas.tsx` component and the need to ensure the `addSubject` function aligns with the database schema. I have the `Subject` type with `color` defined, but the DB doesn't have it, which is the crux of the problem. I'm thinking of suggesting an update to handle the `color` field, or at least handle it as optional with a default. I'll continue debugging in `Disciplinas.tsx`. I am also examining the `App.tsx` file.\n\n\n**Resolving Database Mismatch**\n\nI've decided to remove the problematic `color` field from the insert payload in `Disciplinas.tsx` to align with the provided SQL schema, where the `color` column is not defined. I'll also implement a local color assignment based on index for the UI and enhance the error handling with a `try-catch` block. I've also noticed `fetchUserData` in `App.tsx` has no color handling. So I'll also fix that.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
