      "text": "**Investigating Access Loss**\n\nI'm currently focused on the user's access issue, specifically `ralysonriccelli@gmail.com`. The application uses Supabase for authentication. My current thoughts are centered on how the user might regain access to the application, considering there's a login component, a dashboard, and an admin panel to consider. I am working on the potential recovery mechanisms.\n\n\n**Analyzing Recovery Options**\n\nI've considered several access recovery methods. Analyzing the code, the application lacks a \"Forgot Password\" feature, which seems like the most user-friendly solution. However, there's the manual SQL workaround from `Login.tsx`, possible email confirmation issues, and the admin intervention route. I am inclined to develop a \"Forgot Password\" flow as a more robust solution, as the current options are less ideal.\n\n\n**Implementing Password Reset**\n\nI'm now prioritizing UI changes to include a \"Forgot Password\" feature directly on `Login.tsx`. This involves a button triggering Supabase's password reset flow. For `ralysonriccelli@gmail.com`, I plan to suggest they use this feature. However, I'm also considering the user's likely admin status, so I'll also explore the \"Manual SQL\" trick as a fallback, given Supabase email limits are a possibility.\n\n\n**Adding Password Reset Functionality**\n\nI'm now integrating a \"Reset Password\" UI into `Login.tsx`. I'll introduce `isResettingPassword` state and a `handleResetPassword` method. I'm also ensuring robust error handling for Supabase error codes, especially considering the user's situation. I'll make the manual SQL solution more prominent, too. This is being implemented as the preferred solution, alongside the planned addition of a \"Forgot Password\" button.\n\n\n",
