      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Troubleshooting Login Issues**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Login.tsx` component, specifically the `signInWithPassword` call. I'm investigating why I can't log into the registered account, even after disabling \"Confirm email\" in Supabase. The system is not permitting login, and I need to identify the root cause.\n\n\n**Analyzing Login Robustness**\n\nI've shifted my attention to making the login process more resilient. I'm focusing on providing clearer feedback to the user. My thoughts are centering on distinguishing between \"Invalid login credentials\" versus potential account issues to guide the user effectively. I should also check to confirm that the stale error states aren't appearing in the UI. I also plan to update the `handleDemoAccess` logic for increased clarity.\n\n\n**Investigating Confirmation Bypass**\n\nI'm now digging into potential client-side blocks within `Login.tsx`. I noticed a check for confirmed emails that might be causing trouble, even if Supabase settings changed. Specifically, I'm checking the `email_confirmed_at` value in `auth.users` to confirm if it is null or not. I'm focusing on handling situations where the user disabled email confirmation *after* the account was created. I also plan to add a visual indicator during the \"Logging in...\" state, and improving the error messages. I'm also planning some improvements in the `App` component.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on improving the user experience during login. I want to improve the transition and state handling. I'm focusing on parsing errors, and adding a clear \"Troubleshooting\" section in the `Login` component, especially for cases where confirmation issues persist after the setting change. I need to make the process smoother, especially when the user is trying to log in with an unconfirmed account.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
