    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Admin Capabilities**\n\nOkay, I'm diving into the current codebase now. I need to figure out the best way to integrate administrative user creation and management features. The goal is to allow administrators to add, modify, and delete other users, and edit the pre-defined syllabus templates (editais). I'm considering existing authentication structures to leverage for this.\n\n\n**Integrating Admin Features**\n\nOkay, I've got a clearer picture now. I'm focusing on integrating the `Admin` component based on the `user.role` state defined in `App.tsx`. The goal is to conditionally render an \"Admin\" tab in the sidebar navigation.  I also see that I need to provide a mechanism for a user to *become* an admin, perhaps through a role or email check.  I'm making a note to ensure proper integration of the `Admin` component into the app's structure, focusing on a secure and accessible admin interface. I'm digging deeper into how the existing navigation is set up.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Control**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing the \"admin\" page navigation option. I've realized I need to add an 'admin' case to the `currentPage` switch. I am also implementing a sidebar navigation update, conditionally displaying an \"Gestão\" button if the user's role is 'admin'. My immediate next steps involve fixing the `Admin` component's integration within `App.tsx` and figuring out the best way to handle admin role assignment, considering the Supabase setup. I'm leaning toward a hardcoded super admin check or maybe trusting the SQL script to work.\n\n\n**Refining Admin States**\n\nOkay, I'm streamlining the `App.tsx` file now, focusing on the admin state management. I'm adding `admin_users` and `admin_editais` (or leveraging existing ones) within `App.tsx`, and ensuring the renderPage function includes the `Admin` component. The sidebar will conditionally display the admin link based on the user's role. I need to make sure the Admin component can manage and save data back to Supabase. I'm leaning toward hardcoding admin access for the provided email during testing.\n\n\n**Refining Admin Component**\n\nOkay, I'm now updating the `App.tsx` file to handle the Admin tab and logic. I've realized I need to fetch all user profiles from Supabase if the current user is an admin. The goal is to get the `profiles` data, not rely on `auth.users`, since the direct access isn't available from the client SDK. Then, I need to update `Admin.tsx` to handle fetching and displaying the user profiles for management, and create a toggle for users and editais. Also, I need to add admin promotion logic, maybe hardcoding it.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Bootstrap**\n\nI'm now integrating the bootstrap admin user functionality. I'll hardcode a check for `ralysonriccelli@gmail.com` to force admin role assignment, and add 'admin\\_users' and 'admin\\_editais' to `currentPage`. The sidebar will conditionally render \"Gestão de Usuários\" and \"Gestão de Editais\" when the user is an admin. Additionally, I need to focus on fetching and displaying user profiles from Supabase. I'll be updating `App.tsx` and the `Admin.tsx` components. My plan is to display user management and edital management in the Admin dashboard.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
