  {
    "id": 283,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Revisiting Bulk Edits**\n\nI'm focusing on re-enabling the multi-topic editing feature. I recall this was present in prior iterations, allowing admin users to adjust subjects efficiently. This functionality is key for streamlined data management, and I'm investigating the best approach for restoration.\n\n\n**Analyzing Topic Input Methods**\n\nI've examined the topic handling in both admin and user-facing components. It appears the admin interface, within the \"isCreatingEdital\" modal, already has a working textarea-based approach for bulk topic entry. The `components/Admin.tsx` file provides a textarea, as I recall, where each line defines a topic. Now, I'm verifying the input method in the user \"Disciplinas\" component to verify if that matches.\n\n\n**Implementing Bulk Editing**\n\nI'm focused on integrating a bulk topic editing feature within the user's \"Disciplinas\" component. I'm exploring adding a toggle or dedicated modal to allow users to input multiple topics at once, likely through a textarea. The goal is to replicate the admin interface's bulk input method, which I remember uses a textarea for efficient topic entry. The single-topic method is currently available, but now I'm shifting to a bulk addition method, as requested.\n\n\n**Refining Subject Editing**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the user's need for bulk subject customization within the \"Disciplinas\" component. My plan involves enhancing `components/Disciplinas.tsx` by adding a \"Bulk Edit\" button adjacent to the \"Add Topic\" field for each subject. Upon clicking, a textarea will appear, pre-populated with the subject's current topics, allowing for efficient editing and updates to the Supabase database. I'm focusing on adopting similar textarea logic from `Admin.tsx`.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Interface**\n\nI'm now focusing on the user's needs in the `Disciplinas.tsx` component. I realized the existing single-topic input is insufficient for efficient bulk editing. My current plan is to add a \"Bulk Edit\" option, displaying a textarea for the respective subject ID when activated. I'll maintain the current single input for single-topic updates. I'll keep the plan to make the admin component easy to manage editals.\n\n\n**Evaluating Implementation Strategies**\n\nI'm now weighing the best approach for enabling bulk topic editing. Initially, I planned to add a toggle for \"Bulk Mode\" in `Disciplinas.tsx`, but I'm leaning toward a smarter `addTopic` function that can handle multi-line input directly, or a dedicated UI in the `Disciplinas` page. I've re-examined the `Admin.tsx` code, and I see it already has the core textarea-based functionality for bulk input, which will inform my decisions in enhancing the main page.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769147502,
      "nanos": 215000000
