      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Delete Functions**\n\nI'm currently focused on pinpointing all the button instances with trash can icons that trigger delete actions. The goal is to identify these and integrate a confirmation alert before any actual deletion occurs. I'm carefully reviewing the code to ensure I haven't missed any delete triggers.\n\n\n**Refining Delete Implementation**\n\nI'm now focusing on refining the delete functions across the specified components to ensure consistent confirmation behavior. I've identified that `deleteTopic` lacks a confirmation prompt and will be implementing one. I'm also ensuring the existing confirmation in `deleteSubject` is sufficient and matches our standards. The rest of the functions are next on my list!\n\n\n**Implementing Delete Confirmations**\n\nI've just added confirmation prompts to several more delete functions to standardize the behavior. `deleteTopic` now has a confirmation, and I've ensured `deleteUser` has a robust one. Additionally, I wrapped the delete logic for edital items and subjects within confirmation functions. I also implemented a confirmation check within `deleteTopicFromEdital`. The goal is to fully implement a consistent approach before moving on to the remaining functions.\n\n\n",
