    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Developing Admin Privileges**\n\nI've successfully implemented basic user management restoration, restricted to admin access only. Login/logout and subject CRUD functionality are stable. Mock CRUD operations are working smoothly, with previous fixes implemented. I'm focusing on ensuring robust admin control within the platform.\n\n\n**Refining User Roles**\n\nI'm now integrating user roles into the system: visitor, student, and administrator. I'm focusing on ensuring the application, especially `App.tsx` and `Admin.tsx`, correctly handles role-based access and permissions. The navigation menu will be role-sensitive. The login process will assign default roles. I've updated the `types.ts` file. I'm leveraging a Supabase `profiles` table. The goal is to match previous architectural style. Admin controls for status and role changing are also being implemented.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Management**\n\nI'm now focusing on `App.tsx` and `Admin.tsx` to handle more complete user data. I need to update `fetchAllUsers` to include roles and status and pass `allUsers` to the `Admin` component. Within `Admin.tsx`, I'll implement role selection and status toggles, persisting the updates to the Supabase `profiles` table. I'm updating the `User` type in `types.ts` to support roles, and I'll clean the tables. I'm also reviewing the legacy code to use as a baseline, and make the Admin interface reflect existing style guidelines.\n\n\n",
