'm assigning a `newId` to each subject and `id` to each topic. I'm now writing the Supabase interaction logic.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Import Function**\n\nI've completed implementing the `importEdital` function. It now properly generates new IDs for subjects and topics, handles duplicate subject names, and updates the subject state. I've integrated a success/error message with alerts and incorporated proper error handling in a `try...catch...finally` block to manage loading states effectively. I'm importing the `colors` array directly from `Disciplinas.tsx` line 44, and reviewed `PredefinedEdital` to ensure correct typing with `types.ts`. I will place this function after the definition of `addSubject` in the `Disciplinas.tsx` file.\n\n\n**Refactoring the ID Generation**\n\nI'm now focusing on ID management within `importEdital`. I realize I must regenerate topic IDs to avoid potential conflicts with predefined edital data. I've updated the function and am integrating it into `Disciplinas.tsx`.\n\n\n\n**Integrating the Edit Functions**\n\nI'm now integrating the edit functions. I've placed the definitions within `Disciplinas.tsx` and am verifying that the subject, topic edit, and log functionalities are working as intended. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity and correct state updates within the component, specifically ensuring the `setSubjects` function works correctly. I am also currently working on the edit state for `bulkEdit`.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Progress Tracking**\n\nI'm now integrating state variables for progress tracking: `ProgressTopic`, `progMinutes`, `progAttempted`, and `progCorrect`. I've also incorporated the `colors` array. I'm reviewing the `addSubject` function to see if it needs modification for the additional data, since it currently only handles `name` and `topics`. I'm starting to update the `importEdital` logic for the new tracking system.\n\n\n\n**Updating the Import Function**\n\nI'm now integrating Supabase into the import. I'm modifying the `importEdital` function, and I've focused on directly inserting the new subject data into the 'subjects' table in Supabase. I'm using `supabase.from('subjects').insert()` with the new `name` and `topics` data and I'm ensuring there are unique IDs. I have also added error handling.\n\n\n**Refining the Subject Deletion**\n\nI'm working on refining the `deleteSubject` function within `Disciplinas.tsx`. I've integrated a confirmation dialog before deletion. The function now filters the `subjects` state, updates the `expandedSubject` state if necessary, and attempts a deletion in Supabase. I'm focusing on improved error handling within the Supabase interaction using `try...catch` blocks to address issues with the delete operation.\n\n\n**Refining the Update Function**\n\nI'm now implementing the `updateSubjectData` and `addTopicProgress` functions. The `updateSubjectData` function now updates both the local state and Supabase with the new data. I'm focusing on error handling using try/catch blocks within the Supabase interaction. For the `addTopicProgress` function, I'm updating the local state with the new progress data of the topics in the subjects. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity with both methods.\n\n\n**Refining the Update Function**\n\nI'm now implementing the `deleteTopic` function to enhance subject management. I've integrated a confirmation dialog before topic deletion to prevent accidental removals. The function now filters the `topics` state and updates the database, focusing on robust error handling to address any Supabase interaction issues within `try...catch` blocks. Also the `renameSubject` and `renameTopic` functions have been added to improve subject names and topics names.\n\n\n**Implementing Topic Functions**\n\nI'm now implementing the topic functions, namely `editTopic`, `addTopic`, and `toggleTopic`. I'm integrating logic to update topic titles, add new topics, and toggle topic completion status. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency by updating both local state and Supabase with each action, using asynchronous calls and error handling.\n\n\n**Refining the Topic Actions**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing and testing `toggleTopic`, which updates topic completion, and `saveBulkTopics`, to efficiently add or update multiple topics within a subject. I'm verifying the Supabase interaction and state updates for data consistency, with the implementation of a more concise code using the `updated` variable.\n\n\n\n**Integrating the UI Elements**\n\nI'm now integrating the user interface elements. I'm focusing on the integration of progress tracking with the UI and ensuring seamless state management. I'm currently integrating the logic for conditional coloring based on progress percentages into the progress bar.\n\n\n**Integrating the Subject Add**\n\nI'm now integrating the subject add functionality into the UI, specifically the input field and button. I'm focusing on handling user input for subject names, including a disabled state for the button when the name is empty or while loading. I am also currently verifying the enter key press functionality.\n\n\n\n**Refining the UI Integration**\n\nI'm now refining the UI, specifically the subject component, adding the conditional logic for UI elements such as `SubjectMenu`, and incorporating the inline edit of subjects. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity and responsiveness, making sure that there are no conflicts between functions and the UI.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Edit Function**\n\nI'm now integrating inline editing for subject names within the UI. I'm focusing on the logic to toggle between display and input modes and to handle saving the updated subject name. I am ensuring that the correct subject ID is passed to the `renameSubject` function when changes are saved or when the user presses Enter. I've also implemented conditional rendering and styling for the edit mode.\n\n\n**Integrating the Subject Actions**\n\nI'm now integrating the subject actions UI elements, including the delete and expand/collapse buttons. I'm focusing on ensuring proper event propagation, visual feedback, and correct state management for deletions and expansions. I'm integrating the `deleteSubject` and `isExpanded` state with the visual representation of the subject.\n\n\n**Refining the Bulk Edit UI**\n\nI'm currently focusing on the bulk edit functionality UI. I'm ensuring data consistency and responsiveness, particularly integrating conditional rendering. I'm refining the UI for the bulk edit section, ensuring the `saveBulkTopics` function updates correctly. Also, I'm integrating the bulk edit logic, including the `saveBulkTopics` function and text area input.\n\n\n**Finalizing the UI Integration**\n\nI'm now integrating the bulk edit UI with the subject component to ensure a seamless and intuitive user experience. I've focused on integrating the input field for bulk edits, the cancel and save buttons within the component. I'm verifying that the correct subject ID is passed to the `saveBulkTopics` function, and that this works in conjunction with the `edit` function for inline modifications.\n\n\n**Implementing the Add Topic Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating the add topic functionality. I am focusing on the event handler for adding topics and ensuring the text input field updates the topic title state. I am also integrating the functionality for key press for an enter key press. I'm verifying the `addTopic` function is properly executed on button click and key press with the corresponding `subject.id`.\n\n\n\n**Integrating the Topic Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating the logic to edit and toggle topics within the UI. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency with state and Supabase updates. Specifically, I'm integrating the implementation of the `editTopic`, `addTopic`, and `toggleTopic` functions in the existing code.\n\n\n\n**Refining the UI Integration**\n\nI'm now focusing on refining topic stats. I need to make the progress and question stats UI more responsive, integrating `studyHours` for better tracking and display. I'm verifying the display of hours and questions attempted, considering the current implementation of `Clock` and `Target` icons.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Enhancements**\n\nI'm working on the responsiveness of topic stats. I'm focusing on UI elements to integrate `studyHours`, ensuring accurate progress and question stats display, considering the `Clock` and `Target` icons.\n\n\n**Integrating the Actions**\n\nI'm now integrating the edit and delete topic functions within the UI. Specifically, I'm integrating the `editTopic` and `deleteTopic` functions within the `Topic.tsx` component, including the inline edit form for updating topic titles and confirmation prompts for deletion. I'm verifying that the correct topic and subject IDs are passed to the associated functions.\n\n\n\n**Enhancing the Progress Input**\n\nI'm now integrating the progress input, specifically the minutos (minutes) and feitas (attempted) values, within the UI for each topic. I'm focusing on ensuring these inputs update the local state correctly and that the changes trigger updates in the `Topic.tsx` component.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Progress Inputs**\n\nI'm now integrating the progress input fields for `Acertos` and updating the state variables within the UI, specifically for each topic. I'm focusing on ensuring these inputs correctly update the local state and trigger the `addTopicProgress` function.\n\n\n**Refining the Error Handling**\n\nI'm now focused on the integration of enhanced error handling. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity and responsiveness, making sure that there are no conflicts between functions and the UI.\n\n\n",
