      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Defining Study Session Inputs**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specific data points needed for each study session. My focus is on the \"Disciplinas\" page and how to best capture the study session details. I am prioritizing a date picker for the study date, a numerical input for study hours, and another for questions attempted. I want to ensure these are intuitive for users.\n\n\n**Refining Progress Tracking**\n\nI've added the crucial \"questions correct\" and \"hit rate %\" metrics for progress visualization. I'm focusing on enhancing the \"Add Progress\" form, ensuring it captures date and allows for a more detailed registration history, not just accumulation. The existing implementation already has minutes, questions attempted, and questions correct. I'll integrate the new data points and layout improvements into the existing form flow.\n\n\n**Implementing Date Inputs**\n\nI'm now refactoring `Disciplinas.tsx` to include a date input for progress registration. I've initiated a `progDate` state and will add a date picker, while ensuring the underlying storage and state logic is updated. I will also incorporate the history aspect as well; the idea is to create a true registration system rather than just accumulating values.\n\n\n**Adding Study History**\n\nI'm now integrating study session history. To maintain quick visualization, I'll add a `StudyLog` array to the `Topic` interface in `types.ts`, and update `Disciplinas.tsx` to handle the date in the progress form. This allows for a \"Senior\" feature of study history tracking, with a \"History\" toggle planned for the UI to enhance it further. The existing \"accumulation\" is still in place, but I will improve the UI to be dashboard-like.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI'm now revising my data structure and components. I've realized the `studyLogs` state is underutilized. I will make sure the changes reflect my previous plan. I'm focusing on defining a `TopicLog` interface and integrating it into the `Topic` data structure in `types.ts`, and I'll update the `Disciplinas.tsx` file for a more data-centric approach. I will also incorporate the history aspect as well; the idea is to create a true registration system rather than just accumulating values. I am also implementing the progress history view. I'm prioritizing the form elements needed, and I will be more precise about the data types being used for data entry.\n\n\n**Integrating Study History**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating study session logs. I am updating the data structure to include the new log data and a \"History\" icon for each topic. I'm going to update the `addTopicProgress` to reflect the new updates. I've also identified an empty `onAddLog` prop. I will implement the form for logging study sessions in the UI, and improve the visualization.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
