      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Feature Scope**\n\nOkay, I've decided to streamline the study registration feature. I'm removing the study history button to keep things clean. I'll maintain the core registration fields: study date (using a calendar), time spent, number of questions, and correct answers. My next step will be to handle the case of duplicate topic registrations. I'm focusing on user experience, and reducing redundant complexity.\n\n\n**Simplifying Progress Tracking**\n\nI'm removing the `TopicLog` and simplifying the data structure to track only the latest progress for each topic. My changes involve overwriting existing topic values, not appending to a log. I'm eliminating the history feature and streamlining the user interface. I will also be ensuring the edit form initializes with current topic values, so the user can easily overwrite the data.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Entry Logic**\n\nI'm now clarifying the data entry logic for the study progress form. It appears I'll rewrite topic data instead of appending it, so the form initializes with the current topic values. When the user saves, the values are replaced. I will remove the `TopicLog` and streamline the data structure. I also need to make sure the global stats are not affected by data overwrites. I'm focusing on simplicity and keeping the \"current status\" a primary focus.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
