      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Updating the Revisão Component**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Revisao.tsx` component. My goal is to incorporate all completed topics from every subject into this component. Moreover, I'm integrating milestone calculations based on completion dates, specifically for 7, 15, and 30 days post-completion. I will rely on `lastStudiedAt` data and `completed` status to ensure accuracy.\n\n\n**Refining the Review Mechanism**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the mechanics of review completion within `Revisao.tsx`. The goal is to create a clear \"complete review\" button. The review data entry form must be similar to the form in `Disciplinas.tsx`. Reviews will be binary, marking milestones as done. I'm focusing on how `revisionsDone: number[]` handles the completed milestone indicators. I'm still figuring out the logic for handling revisions and how it connects with milestone calculations.\n\n\n**Integrating Review Data**\n\nI'm now integrating the review data entry. My focus is mirroring the `Disciplinas.tsx` approach for similar data capture: questions, answers, performance, and time spent. Unlike postponable reviews, each review will update a specific milestone. I'm leaning toward updating the topic's overall stats directly, recording which milestone is completed to adjust the totals accordingly.\n\n\n**Clarifying Milestone Updates**\n\nI'm now refining how milestone completion is tracked within `Revisao.tsx`. My previous idea of incrementing the topic stats now feels less aligned with a holistic performance view. I'm leaning toward reflecting the *total* performance of each completed topic. The \"Realizar Revisão\" form's logic will now focus on recording which review milestone is done, and updating the overall topic's statistics based on the review results. The list will show completed topics.\n\n\n**Refining UI/UX for Revisão**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on UI consistency with `Disciplinas.tsx`. The \"Concluir Revisão\" button will trigger an inline form, mirroring the style. I'll make the form allow selecting the completed milestone. Each topic will also show milestone status and an \"Aproveitamento Atual\" badge. Review completion will directly update topic stats, leveraging a form with Date, Time, Questions, and Correct fields, linked to a specific milestone. My goal is to streamline milestone tracking and overall topic performance insights. I will apply this exact UI/UX style to `Revisao.tsx`, but specialized for the 3 milestones.\n\n\n**Implementing Topic Display**\n\nI'm now implementing the display of completed topics from all subjects in `Revisao.tsx`, ensuring robust filtering based on the 'completed' status. I'll also add a quick visual indicator of the topic's overall performance percentage to give the user a rapid assessment. I'm verifying the `types.ts` file for `revisionsDone` and will proceed to integrate the logic for saving reviews.\n\nFor each saved review, I intend to update the `revisionsDone` array, adjust topic totals, and ensure the parent state is correctly updated. I am also checking how the `onAddLog` prop is utilized, and I see from `App.tsx` that it is passed to `Revisao`, so I'll stay consistent with that.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
