nsure the logic overwrites the existing date, and correctly sets to `null` if the field is cleared. I'm also considering the implications of allowing date setting even if a topic isn't marked as \"completed,\" which aligns with the request to \"alterar a data de conclusão\".\n\n\n**Modifying Save Logic**\n\nI'm now refining the `saveTopicProgress` function to accommodate new user interactions. I'll make the input always available and functional, even for incomplete topics. Specifically, I'll update the function to set `completed: true` if a `progConcludedAt` date is provided, ensuring that changing the date always triggers an update and correctly manages null values if the field is cleared. This should ensure the conclusion date is correctly updated, or cleared, depending on user input, and will always be stored in the database.\n\n\n**Clarifying Date Storage**\n\nI'm now focusing on how the conclusion date is stored and handled to ensure alignment with user expectations. I've considered that the user may be seeing an older date interfering with the intended behavior. The current logic uses `concludedAt` as the primary date, prioritizing it over `lastStudiedAt`. I'll update `Disciplinas.tsx` to handle the date directly and avoid potential timezone issues. The user wants the ability to fix mistakes.\n\n\n**Refining Date Formatting**\n\nI'm now implementing explicit date handling within `Disciplinas.tsx` to directly manage `concludedAt`. I've added a string representation and am using a `new Date()` object with the `T12:00:00Z` timezone offset to resolve timezone issues. My code will format the date for consistency. This should correctly manage the date the user sets.\n\n\n**Expanding Field Visibility**\n\nI'm now revising the progress form to always display the \"Data de Conclusão do Tópico (Marco das Revisões)\" field, regardless of topic completion status. The `saveTopicProgress` function will be updated to handle this new behavior. I'll ensure the date updates `co