is to make it clear that modifying \"Data do Estudo\" will update the \"Último Estudo\" information. I'll need to modify `Disciplinas.tsx` to: (1) clearly label \"Data do Estudo\" for editing, (2) ensure that changing \"Data do Estudo\" changes `lastStudiedAt`, and (3) add a helpful notice for users to realize that \"Data do Estudo\" is linked to the \"Último Estudo\". I believe this update streamlines the user's workflow.\n\n\n**Clarifying Overwrite Behavior**\n\nI'm now focusing on clarifying the \"Data do Último Estudo\" field within the `Disciplinas.tsx` file to explicitly highlight its overwriting behavior. The current code uses the date input, `progDate`, which correctly updates `lastStudiedAt`. My core concern is to clearly communicate that the entered date *replaces* the existing \"Último Estudo\" date. The \"Data do Último Estudo\" label is being updated to reflect this clarifying intention. I will check the user instruction for any indication of confusion.\n\n\n**Verifying Date Overwrite**\n\nI'm now confirming the date overwrite behavior within `Disciplinas.tsx`, specifically how `progDate` affects `lastStudiedAt`.  My current check is to ensure that the code explicitly replaces the previous date entry, and it does so correctly. I'm also confirming that logs are *not* broken by this behavior. I'm also reviewing the implementation to ensure \"Data de Conclusão\" and \"Último Estudo\" are clearly presented for user clarity.\n\n\n**Confirming Clear Overwrite**\n\nI am now ensuring the user clearly understands that entering a new \"Data do Estudo\" will overwrite the previous entry for that topic. I need to make the intent clear to the user that the information entered replaces the existing record. I'm focusing on ensuring this clarity through UI adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining Field Management**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the field management within `Disciplinas.tsx`. My current task is to make sure the state variables, including `bulkEditId`, `bulkText`,