ting the Inputs**\n\nI'm now focusing on validating the data input within the progress form. I'm carefully reviewing the number inputs for correct data parsing and state updates. I have checked for proper type consistency for all inputs, making sure the user inputs are correctly interpreted. I've also validated the save functionality of the button to ensure the progress information is saved appropriately.\n\n\n**Verifying Full Component**\n\nI'm now methodically verifying the complete `Disciplinas.tsx` component implementation. I am confirming all functions are correctly implemented and integrated. I am ensuring that the component, including UI and functionality, is comprehensive and free of missing components. I've also checked the `geminiService.ts` for the correct model name and verified the latency guidelines. I am now proceeding with a final code review for overall integrity.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Settings**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the configurations for the Gemini SDK, specifically focusing on the `gemini-3-pro-preview` model. I've noted that the maximum context length, or `thinkingBudget`, is 32768, which is not being explicitly set in the current implementation. I'm verifying how this affects the `geminiService.ts` calls and whether there are any impacts on model performance. I will be checking on how it is being used in the code.\n\n\n**Finalizing Functionality Implementation**\n\nI'm now integrating the progress-saving and update functionality within `Disciplinas.tsx`. I am focusing on the complete save button integration. I'm verifying the correct data formatting. I'm also now proceeding with UI adjustments for edge cases to improve responsiveness. Now the focus is on validation and formatting.\n\n\n**Integrating Progress Inputs**\n\nI'm now integrating the form's `newTopicTitle`, `loading`, `isCatalogOpen`, and progress state variables (`activeProgressTopic`, `progDate`, `progHours`, `progMinutes`, `progAttempted`, `progCorrect`). I'm now integrating the `colors` array. The focus now is on integrating the `updateSubjectInDb` function, which handles updates to the database.\n\n\n**Integrating Subject Deletion**\n\nI'm now integrating subject deletion into the UI, ensuring confirmation prompts and state updates are working. I am now incorporating database deletion using Supabase, along with appropriate error handling and UI feedback, based on the previous implementation. I'm verifying data consistency after database operations, considering potential race conditions.\n\n\n**Refining Progress Saving**\n\nI'm now refining the `saveTopicProgress` function to ensure correct date formatting and calculations. I am validating that it accurately extracts date and time information. I am also verifying that the time in minutes is correctly calculated and updated in the topics. I'm focusing on ensuring data integrity when updating subjects and topics.\n\n\n**Refining Subject Updates**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the `toggleTopic` function for correct subject data manipulation and database updates. I've confirmed state updates for topic completion status, concluding and last studied dates. The focus is on the correct integration with `updateSubjectInDb`. I'm now proceeding with the final review.\n\n\n**Refining Data Integrity**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on data integrity, especially within the topic manipulation functions. I'm focusing on the `toggleTopic` logic to ensure that updates correctly reflect changes in the database and UI state. Specifically, I'm verifying accurate update of the study time and checking the updates in the `concludedAt` field. I am making sure the changes are persistent.\n\n\n**Analyzing Deletion Function**\n\nI'm now carefully analyzing the topic deletion function. I've focused on the confirmation dialog, the `filter` method for state updates, and the asynchronous database interaction. I'm confirming that the `updateSubjectInDb` call is correctly implemented and correctly updates the state