      "text": "**Analyzing Component Changes**\n\nOkay, I'm diving into the `Revisao.tsx` component now, focusing on the differences between the existing code and the new model. I'm making sure any other adjustments needed, like the Recharts error fix, are incorporated alongside these updates. I am using the `subjects` property from the source file.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Code Synchronization**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on synchronizing the provided `Revisao.tsx` update with the existing code, accounting for discrepancies. The provided `Revisao.tsx` model introduces a shift to using `t.lastStudiedAt`, which I need to integrate, although the old code used `concludedAt`. I am starting with the `Revisao.tsx` updates, and will review the `Dashboard.tsx` later. I've also noted state management changes for the topic review.\n\n\n**Implementing Milestone Choices**\n\nI've decided to incorporate milestone selection, allowing choices for 7, 15, or 30 days. I'll use `topic.lastStudiedAt` as the anchor date for these calculations, making the UI work by using cards for completed topics. There will be a \"Concluir Revisão\" button to show the editing panel, a progress bar and status labels for milestones such as \"Concluída\", \"Atrasada\", and others. Also, I've got `getAllCompletedTopics` working which filters, sorts by recent `completed` and `lastStudiedAt`, and the `saveStats` now incorporates all the updates. It will also update the app using `setSubjects`.\n\n\n**Confirming Component Imports**\n\nI am now confirming the necessary imports for `Revisao.tsx`. The model includes `RefreshCcw`, `Bell`, and others. I'll verify these match existing imports and ensure everything is included correctly. I already confirmed the Recharts fix is in the provided \"Existing files\". It looks like I am ready to review the new code and ensure it is integrated properly.\n\n\n",
