  {
    "id": 426,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Component Revisions**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Disciplinas.tsx` component. The target model dictates inclusion of an \"Edital Verticalizado\" section, complete with a title and description. I'm also revising the header for enhanced functionality, specifically integrating a \"Catalog\" button for user navigation.\n\n\n**Integrating Model Aesthetics**\n\nI've integrated the model's design cues into `Disciplinas.tsx`. I've added a compact \"Add Subject\" input, implemented subject cards with progress indicators, bulk import, and delete buttons. The subject cards also expand to display associated topics. Furthermore, I've styled with indigo accents, rounded borders, and shadow effects. I've also incorporated the bulk import and global catalog modals.\n\n\n**Implementing Model Features**\n\nI'm now focused on translating the model's features into code for `Disciplinas.tsx`. The revised header layout with \"Edital Verticalizado\" and the new button group is implemented. The subject card's updated design, including the indicator bar, progress text, and quick actions, is in place. I'm also ensuring the bulk import modal and the catalog modal function correctly, and that Supabase calls within `handleSubjectUpdate` and `addSubject` remain intact. Finally, the offline detection is preserved.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Integration**\n\nI'm now integrating the \"Registrar Desempenho\" feature, ensuring it aligns with the updated topic row design, since removing it would break core functionality. I'm also ensuring the Supabase ID logic is maintained for `addSubject` and `handleSubjectUpdate`, while integrating the \"Edital Verticalizado\" section and button group as requested.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
