    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Visualizing Study Data**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating a concise display of the study data directly within the `Disciplinas` component. The initial \"Registrar\" button will remain but will now be accompanied by a small, summarized view of study sessions – including date, time, and relevant performance metrics, to provide users with a quick overview. I'm exploring different layout options to ensure clarity and minimal visual clutter.\n\n\n**Integrating Topic Metrics**\n\nI'm now integrating study metrics directly into the topic rows within `Disciplinas.tsx`. My focus is on concise display. I am incorporating a \"Stats\" area to display study time, attempts, and correct answers, and I'm adding an efficiency percentage. I'm leveraging icons for clarity and plan to use a progress bar or badge for efficiency. The layout is being designed for a professional and compact appearance within the current \"Edital Verticalizado\" design.\n\n\n**Refining Topic Display**\n\nI'm now refining the presentation of each topic row in `Disciplinas.tsx`. I've added a more compact and informative display of key data. Now, a study summary line will be conditionally shown, it displays the \"last studied\" date, study time, and questions attempted. Icons are employed for better comprehension and a cleaner user interface. The styling and layout are designed for a professional and unobtrusive look within the existing vertical design.\n\n\n**Displaying Last Studied**\n\nI'm now integrating the last study session information directly within the topic row. My focus is on concise and clear presentation. I'm adding the date of the last study session, total study time, and the number of questions attempted, all displayed using a clean and compact layout. Icons are being used to improve readability. I'm aiming for a subtle but informative display.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
