  {
    "id": 436,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Visualizing Topic Data**\n\nI'm focusing on enhancing the \"Disciplinas\" component. My current thought process revolves around visualizing data for each topic listed. I intend to display key metrics like date, time, questions answered, correct answers, and hit rate. Additionally, I'm considering how best to visually represent a topic's completion status.\n\n\n**Refining Date Handling**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the date-handling logic within `toggleTopic` in `Disciplinas.tsx`. Previously I incorrectly assumed the dates being used as registration dates. Now, I understand that if a topic is *already* registered as completed (meaning there's a registered date stored), I need to respect that date, and avoid overwriting it. My update will include more fine-grained date handling to ensure accurate data visualization, specifically considering registered conclusion dates. I need to make sure I represent the dates accurately for data, time, questions, corrects, and hits.\n\n\n**Updating Topic Summary**\n\nI'm now focusing on ensuring the topic UI displays a concise summary: \"data, tempo, questões, acertos, aproveitamento.\" If a topic is marked as done, I'll display the registered date if available, otherwise use the date it was last studied, or the concluded date if present. The `saveTopicProgress` function is key here, setting `lastStudiedAt`, and the UI needs to reflect that, taking into account scenarios involving manually registered completion dates as well. I'm refining `components/Disciplinas.tsx`.\n\n\n**Enhancing Stat Display**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on improving the presentation of topic statistics. I intend to create a clearer, more professional display format for the five key metrics: data, tempo, questões, acertos, and aproveitamento. My focus is on ensuring the \"Concluir\" checkbox's behavior aligns with user expectations. I need to make the logic in `toggleTopic` smarter, so it respects manually registered completion dates and doesn't overwrite them with the current date, ensuring data accuracy.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769193795,
      "nanos": 50000000
    },
