  {
    "id": 439,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Project Aesthetics**\n\nI'm currently focused on the *Disciplinas* (Subjects) page. My goal is to add a data visualization under topics that gives a quick overview of study progress: date, time spent, questions attempted, correct answers, and hit rate. I need to figure out the best visual representation for this. I want to keep it clean and intuitive for the user.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Aggregation**\n\nI've realized the need for precise data handling. When a user marks a topic complete, I should use the recorded completion date for visualization, not the current date. I'm also addressing the non-cumulative data. Instead of accumulating study time, I'm opting to replace previous entries with the latest recorded session data. I'm focusing on robust Supabase integration for data functions and will create a dedicated TopicSummary component to display the information clearly. I also want to use the \"Concurseiro Pro AI\" theme.\n\n\n**Interpreting \"Not Cumulative\"**\n\nI've clarified the intent behind \"not cumulative\" – it refers to replacing current study state data rather than summing it. This means `studyTimeMinutes`, `questionsAttempted`, and `questionsCorrect` are updated with the *latest* session's values, not added to existing totals. I'm focusing on UI updates: compact badges for topic stats with a contrast between \"Completed\" and \"In Progress\" states, plus a refined registration modal. I'll also modify the save functions in `Disciplinas.tsx`.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769193945,
      "nanos": 314000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769193954,
      "nanos": 3000000
    }
