      "nanos": 569000000
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 443,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Defining User Roles**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining user roles for this environment. I've broken it down into two core roles: Administrator and Student. The Administrator will have complete access, including user and catalog management, while the Student will have standard access. I am now exploring further differentiation of these roles.\n\n\n**Expanding Access Levels**\n\nI'm now expanding the access levels, introducing a \"Visitor\" role alongside \"Administrator\" and \"Student.\" This new role gets demo access, implemented through a \"Demo\" button in `Login.tsx`. I need to ensure restricted functionality for Visitors, perhaps read-only access to Supabase. Furthermore, I'm working on the Administrator UI, aiming for a professional \"Admin Dashboard\" feel with user stats, a refined table, status badges, role switchers, and action buttons. I also plan for high-end UI patterns for visual polish.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control**\n\nI'm now implementing an `AccessControl` utility to wrap features based on user roles. I'm focusing on success/error feedback through toasts for admin actions. In `App.tsx`, I'm refining the sidebar to show the \"Admin\" section only to admins and adding a \"Visitor\" banner if the role is visitor. I'm also ensuring that admin-specific pages are unreachable for other roles. Further, I'm working to refine the user management table in `Admin.tsx`, aiming to add filters/search and improve the \"Edit Edital\" experience. In `Login.tsx`, I'm verifying the correct assignment of the \"Visitor\" role upon button click. Finally, I need to check for changes to `types.ts`, and am thinking about functional patterns and web design considerations.\n\n\n**Refining Visitor Experience**\n\nI'm now adding a \"Restricted\" overlay for Visitors to clearly indicate demo mode, and will add conditional sidebar items in `App.tsx`. The admin user list in `Admin.tsx` needs an \"Enterprise\" redesign, focusing on a powerful control grid with user metrics. I'm also ensuring the demo user role in `Login.tsx` is fixed as \"Visitor\". I'm planning to disable specific \"Save\" actions for Visitors with a professional \"Unlock Full Version\" toast. I am also planning the side bar now.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769194704,
      "nanos": 569000000
