    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Study Registration**\n\nI'm currently focused on dissecting the \"Registrar Estudo\" functionality within `components/Disciplinas.tsx`. My primary goal is to understand how the study date registration modal is triggered and how it interacts with the backend. I'm noting the existing code's structure for the logic and data flow to replicate the behavior. I am also planning on checking which components use the date.\n\n\n**Refining Progress Tracking**\n\nI've been examining the flow of study data. The 'Registrar Estudo' button correctly triggers the modal, allowing entry of study time and question results. I can see that the `saveTopicProgress` function is updating the `topic` state and triggering `onAddLog` to save to Supabase. Now, I see the user might want a date field. The existing system seems to manage `progDate` and `lastStudiedAt` but I'm looking to enhance date handling for this purpose. I am working to ensure full integration with Supabase.\n\n\n**Enhancing Log Insertion**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the `study_logs` insertion. I've confirmed the database expects `topic_id` and `subject_id` (snake_case), which I'll be implementing correctly. I'm also planning to incorporate a \"Histórico de Estudos\" feature to visualize study dates for each topic. I'm looking to refine the date handling in `addStudyLog` so it can handle a user-provided date, rather than always today's date, and I plan to enhance the modal and make it more visually clear. Also, I'm making sure `lastStudiedAt` is correctly updated in the `subjects` table.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
