      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Date Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on the \"Edital Vertical\" page, specifically the \"Topics\" section. My central thought concerns the \"conclude\" button's function. I need to ensure the recorded date for topic completion is user-defined (from `lastStudiedAt` or similar input) instead of an automatic timestamp. This will improve accuracy and user experience.\n\n\n**Revisiting Toggle Behavior**\n\nI'm now reconsidering the `toggleTopic` functionality, triggered by direct checkmark clicks. Previously, the system defaulted to the current date on completion, but the user wants to preserve a user-specified date. This poses a challenge, as the user might not have explicitly provided a completion date via the modal. If there's no pre-existing completion date, should a date be created or should it remain empty?\n\n\n**Analyzing Date Implications**\n\nI'm now focusing on what happens when a user toggles a topic as complete. My primary concern is how to handle the `lastStudiedAt` date when a checkmark is clicked. I'm exploring the implications of \"não incluir a data atual,\" meaning \"don't include the current date\". If there's an existing `lastStudiedAt`, I should keep it; if not, I'm considering options: prompt for a date, or leave it unset, consistent with the user's intent to \"maintain the registered date\". This requires revisiting the `toggleTopic` functionality and considering that \"Concluir\" (Conclude) indicates completion.\n\n\n**Adjusting `toggleTopic` Logic**\n\nI've revised the `toggleTopic` function to avoid automatic `lastStudiedAt` updates. It now preserves existing dates or leaves the field null, as the user desires. The primary intention is to maintain the user's registered date if available, or leave it unset if not. This aligns with the \"do not include the current date\" directive. Now, the `lastStudiedAt` field is only modified when a study session is registered through the modal, or is `saveTopicProgress` being invoked. I will now re-check the operation of `saveTopicProgress` for proper behavior.\n\n\n**Refining Update Implementation**\n\nI'm now implementing the latest directive within `Disciplinas.tsx`, specifically revisiting `toggleTopic`. My focus is to completely prevent the automatic inclusion of the current date for the `lastStudiedAt` field when a topic is concluded via the checkmark. I'm taking the \"não incluir a data atual\" command literally and removing the date assignment. If there's no pre-existing completion date, it should remain empty, as opposed to setting a default. I'm also ensuring the code respects the `progDate` value.\n\n\n",
