      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Exam Data Structures**\n\nI'm currently fleshing out the Supabase schema modifications to fully accommodate *Mock Exams*. I'm focusing on how this will work, following the Master Catalog update; specifically, ensuring the mock exam data is saved correctly. I'm taking into consideration any potential issues in the underlying data structure in my current thinking.\n\n\n**Defining Mock Exam Structure**\n\nI've specified the `mocks` table's structure, including `id`, `title`, `date`, `score`, `total_questions`, `subject_performance`, and `user_id`. I'm verifying the `user_id` FK constraint. Also, I'm documenting the need to enable RLS and create policies. The existing code uses both snake_case and camelCase, which I'm considering.\n\n\n**Prioritizing SQL Structure**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the SQL for the `mocks` table, aiming for a clean implementation that directly answers the \"Simulados\" request. I've decided on using `bigserial` for the `id` column. I'm focusing on dropping conflicting policies and creating a \"Manage own mocks\" policy to enable RLS. I've confirmed that `profiles` and `subjects` tables already exist, so I just need to add the `mocks` part. I am focusing on generating the SQL code for this table.\n\n\n**Validating RLS Policies**\n\nI've just revisited the `App.tsx` file and verified the camelCase-to-snake_case mapping, confirming it's correct for the mock exams data. I am feeling confident with the policies for the `mocks` table, which includes RLS and the \"Manage own mocks\" policy using `auth.uid() = user_id`. I've added `score`, `total_questions`, `subject_performance`, `user_id`, and `created_at` with default values and types for the SQL table. I'm satisfied the mocks structure is now complete.\n\n\n**Verifying Table Existence**\n\nI've reviewed the code snippet, confirming the `insert` query looks correct for the `mocks` table, which includes `title`, `date`, `score`, `total_questions`, `subject_performance`, and `user_id`. I'm now zeroing in on verifying the table actually exists within the user's Supabase project. I'm also planning to check if the `study_logs` table exists, because `App.tsx` fetches from it, which would also cause errors. I intend to generate the SQL for these tables, if necessary.\n\n\n**Finalizing SQL Solution**\n\nI'm now generating the SQL for both `mocks` and `study_logs` tables to ensure a complete solution as I proceed. I'm verifying the `id` column type and the code usage. My plan includes checking for any mismatches in the existing code. Everything seems aligned, but I'll ensure I provide a clear SQL code block. I believe this will ensure the code works as expected.\n\n\n",
