      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Verifying Data Persistence**\n\nI'm now focusing on the \"Revisões\" (Revisions) page and confirming that it's successfully saving data to Supabase. I'm verifying that the `StudySession` objects (logs) are being transmitted via `onAddLog` as intended. The aim is to ensure data consistency across the application. I've begun to trace and validate the data flow from the front-end to Supabase.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Updates**\n\nI've pinpointed a critical issue in `Revisao.tsx`. While minutes spent on revisions are being logged, the milestones within `revisionsDone` aren't being synced to Supabase. Updating the `subjects` state locally isn't enough; the `topics` array update, which contains the revision status, needs to trigger `handleSubjectUpdate` in `Disciplinas.tsx` for proper persistence. This inconsistency means that upon refresh, progress could be lost since the database won't have the updated milestones. This relates to updates from `Disciplinas.tsx` to the `subjects` table.\n\n\n",
