      "nanos": 295000000
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 515,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Envisioning Admin Page Needs**\n\nI'm currently focused on the \"Comunidade\" page redesign. My primary goal is to empower admins with robust user management tools. I'm prioritizing the inclusion of real-time online status indicators, a clear view of blocked users, and intuitive role management capabilities. Editing and deletion features are also essential for complete control.\n\n\n**Refining Admin Functionality**\n\nI'm now diving deeper into the required updates to `Admin.tsx` and `App.tsx`. The core work involves implementing edit and delete capabilities for user profiles. I'll need to modify the SQL schema to include `last_seen` or a similar field if we go for a \"who's online\" indicator. This includes ensuring the Admin has appropriate policies to view *all* profiles, instead of just their own. My current thinking is centered around adding edit and delete buttons to the UI, alongside visual cues for user status.\n\n\n**Updating SQL Database Schema**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the database schema. My immediate focus is enhancing the SQL policies. I've identified the need for a comprehensive view policy for admins to see all user profiles, followed by policies that enable admins to edit and delete user data. I'm also planning to add the `last_seen` column to the profiles table. Next, I'll be focused on writing the code required to implement these changes.\n\n\n**Implementing User Profile Updates**\n\nNow, I'm working to implement the edit and delete functionalities in `Admin.tsx`, including modals and confirmation dialogs. I'm focusing on user status display, and I will be mocking the \"online\" status for now to get the UI running. Then, I will focus on updating the `User` type in `types.ts` to fully sync with the `profiles` table. I'm ensuring `App.tsx` correctly fetches all user profiles.\n\n\n**Adding Admin Controls**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the admin's capabilities over user profiles. I'm prioritizing full CRUD functionality, smooth transitions in the UI for edit/view modes, and high-contrast badges to convey important information. I also need to provide clear loading states for all backend operations to give the admin confidence in the system. Finally, I've outlined the necessary SQL changes to support all admin actions.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
