      "text": "**Considering User Management**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating user management within StudyFlow. I've been given a SQL schema and RLS policies for profiles. My priority is establishing functionality for: online/offline status, blocked users, and user roles. I plan to incorporate user role and status editing, and a delete function for users.\n\n\n**Aligning SQL and App**\n\nOkay, I'm now comparing the provided SQL schema with my previous code suggestions. I need to make sure the app correctly handles the user's defined roles and statuses. I see there's no `last_seen` column, which is essential for \"online\" status, so I'll suggest how to manage that, either in the SQL or in the app. My focus is now on ensuring the app's functionality mirrors the database structure, especially user roles, blocking, and online status, while keeping things as minimal as possible in my updates.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Implementation**\n\nI'm now revising my proposed updates based on existing code. I don't need to change `types.ts`; the types are already good. In `App.tsx`, I'll update the heartbeat logic to use a `last_seen` column. In the `init` function, I will ensure fetching of the user's role and status from the `profiles` table. I'll handle sign-out if the status is \"blocked\". I'll also add fetching of all users for the administrator in `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining Necessary Updates**\n\nI'm now focusing on what is strictly needed for the updates, given the user's prompt. I've reevaluated the approach: I'll refine the `App.tsx` file for session initialization and heartbeat, and create a full administrative interface in `Admin.tsx` file.\n\n\n",
