    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Designing the Platform's Core**\n\nI'm currently focused on the core functionalities of a study platform. User management is a key aspect, encompassing online/blocked status, roles, and privileges, along with the ability to edit and delete users. I also want to make sure the initial pages - *Início*, *Disciplinas*, and *Revisões* - are retained.\n\n\n**Expanding the Application's Scope**\n\nI'm now integrating new features: *Ciclos* for AI-driven study schedules and *Simulados* to track mock exam results. I'm focusing on the frontend, specifically `Ciclos.tsx`, `Revisao.tsx`, `Simulados.tsx`, and `Admin.tsx`, ensuring smooth data fetching and navigation within `App.tsx`. The `Admin.tsx` component is designed to manage both users (\"Membros\") and predefined editals (\"Matrizes\"). I've enabled RLS and implemented triggers for automatic profile creation.\n\n\n**Refining Component Interactions**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the granular details within each component. Specifically, `Disciplinas.tsx` needs to manage the \"user\\_id\" constraint, and I want to ensure the `PredefinedEdital` logic in `Admin.tsx` is completely correct, correcting the prior summary. `App.tsx` requires robust state management for key data and incorporates a heartbeat function for updating user activity. I'm focusing on navigation and Supabase integration across all seven pages.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Enhancements**\n\nI'm now integrating the mock exam result logging into `Simulados.tsx`. Simultaneously, I'm focusing on high-level analytics for the dashboard component, `Dashboard.tsx`, with a plan to leverage Tailwind CSS, Lucide-React icons, glassmorphism, and dark mode support for the UI. I'm also reviewing `PredefinedEdital` types and user roles (`administrator`, `student`, `visitor`) and statuses (`active`, `blocked`). Importantly, when an administrator logs in, I will need to fetch all profiles to populate `allUsers` in `App.tsx`. I'm using Supabase and Gemini.\n\n\n",
