    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering Admin Component Functionality**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Admin` component's capabilities, specifically how it handles new user additions. Right now, the core architecture leverages an `App.tsx` state variable, `currentPage`, to determine the displayed content, rendering the `Admin` component with a `view=\"users\"` prop when appropriate. I must now add code to accommodate new users.\n\n\n**Revising User Creation Strategy**\n\nI'm revisiting the user addition process in `Admin.tsx`. Initially, I was looking at `supabase.auth.admin.createUser`, but I now realize the security implications of that approach on the frontend. I'm pivoting to a \"Add Member\" form using `supabase.auth.signUp`, or a simpler profile insertion, if the API does not allow admin-level creation. My focus is now on the user signup or a direct `profiles` insertion, not the risky admin method.\n\n\n**Refining Signup Implementation**\n\nI'm now honing the \"Add User\" feature in `Admin.tsx`. My current focus is integrating the signup process. I'm leaning toward a form within the `Admin` component. This will ask for email, password, name, role, and status, calling `auth.signUp` for new user creation. I'm aiming for a straightforward implementation, fitting the \"Senior Developer\" persona.\n\n\n**Implementing User Creation Functionality**\n\nI'm now implementing the \"Novo Membro\" (New Member) button within the `Admin` component, focusing on user creation. My plan involves a form inside the component with fields for new user details, and I'll call a `createUser` function to handle the new user process. I also need to make sure to account for possible type errors or missing props as well. I'm going to set up state variable to manage the modal's open/close status, and ensure the styling aligns with the dark mode and glassmorphism. I'm considering the potential impact of `signUp` creating a new session, leaning toward an \"Invite/Create\" flow.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
