    "id": 554,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Initiating Database Setup**\n\nI'm diving into this project with the goal of setting up the Supabase database from the ground up, deleting any existing configurations to ensure a clean slate. I'm focusing on a step-by-step guide. The `App.tsx` file is key as it fetches essential data: `subjects`, `mocks`, `study_logs`, and `study_cycles`.\n\n\n**Defining Core Database Tables**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining the key database tables based on the components and code analysis. My focus is on `profiles` (linked to `auth.users`), `subjects`, `mocks`, `study_logs`, `study_cycles`, and the admin-only `predefined_editais` table. Right now, I'm prioritizing the setup of `profiles` and authentication, including the crucial trigger for automated profile creation on signup. Next, I need to secure the `is_admin()` function.\n\n\n**Implementing Table Structures**\n\nI'm now in the thick of creating those tables, applying constraints, and implementing RLS policies for robust data security. I've got the data definitions for `profiles`, `subjects`, `mocks`, `study_logs`, `study_cycles`, and `predefined_editais` defined. To prevent bugs, I'll set the `is_admin()` function as `SECURITY DEFINER`. For optimization and flexibility, I'll leverage `JSONB` for `topics` and `schedules` while writing clean SQL with helpful comments.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
