    "id": 592,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering Site Aesthetics**\n\nI'm now focusing on re-imagining the interface, emphasizing a website-style approach. I'm starting with the background, aiming for a visual vibe that evokes a cozy, academic setting. I'm thinking of a dim library ambiance with books and coffee, which should enhance the user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Design**\n\nI've decided to replace the initially considered ngtree URL background with a high-quality Unsplash image, specifically matching the dark library aesthetic. The focus is on a dimly lit atmosphere to maintain a futuristic, glassmorphic look with high text contrast. I'm also narrowing the left sidebar to prioritize the data display, and am now generating unique atmospheric background images for each major page, using Unsplash keywords. My plan is to update `index.html` to reflect these changes, including CSS adjustments for the sidebar and glassmorphism.\n\n\n**Implementing Dynamic Backgrounds**\n\nI'm now integrating dynamic background changes into `App.tsx` based on the `currentPage` state. My plan involves reducing the sidebar width and refining layout transitions. I'll ensure `Dashboard.tsx` and `Disciplinas.tsx` are dark-theme compatible, especially considering glassmorphism. For page backgrounds, I've chosen thematic images. \"Início\" will feature a dark library with coffee. \"Disciplinas\" will use old book pages. \"Revisões\" will incorporate a clock, \"Ciclos\" abstract brain/circuits, and \"Simulados\" a pen/paper setup. I intend to adjust the CSS background property to achieve a similar effect to generated content, instead of using `GenerateContent`.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
