w I'm checking `App.tsx` and adding `BarChart2` to the import. I'm focusing on validating the chart components.\n\n\n**Confirming the Imports**\n\nI've just added `BarChart2` to `App.tsx`'s lucide-react import. I made sure to check for potential naming conflicts. I'm now certain that the `BarChart2` icon is accessible across components, as well as the text generation is correct as specified. I'm satisfied the API key is being accessed properly.\n\n\n**Validating Model Selection**\n\nI'm now satisfied that the model selection of `\"gemini-3-pro-preview\"` in `geminiService.ts` is correct for the study cycle generation (text) task, following the recent guidelines. I've reconfirmed that this is the appropriate model and format as per the documentation, ensuring compatibility with the current functionality and the examples provided.\n\n\n**Confirming Correct Configuration**\n\nI'm now focusing on the configuration of `generateContent` in `geminiService.ts`. I realized the property for instructions is `config`, not `instructions`, so I've updated the code accordingly. I've reconfirmed that the `responseSchema` is also correct. I will now revisit the imports in `Dashboard.tsx` and `App.tsx` again.\n\n\n**Revisiting Chart Imports**\n\nOkay, I'm now re-examining `components/Dashboard.tsx` closely. I've re-confirmed that `BarChart2` is used for the icon, specifically on line 189 in the rendered `else` block, not line 170. I'm focusing now on adding the import statement for `BarChart2` from `lucide-react` to resolve the import error. I see that the correct line is 189. I'm going to add that import now.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Imports**\n\nOkay, I'm now certain that the issue in `Dashboard.tsx` is due to the dual import of `BarChart`. It's being imported from `recharts` for the chart rendering, but I was attempting to import `BarChart` from `lucide-react` as well for the icon, leading to the conflict. `BarChart2` from `lucide-react` is the correct solution. I've reconfirmed