rd.tsx` component, carefully examining the rendering of the text content and input for goal editing. I'm verifying the states that control the editing mode and the input field update, including the \"Definir\" button functionality. The goal is to make sure it's accurate.\n\n\n\n**Refining UI Calculations**\n\nI'm now diving into the calculations and display logic of the UI elements in `Dashboard.tsx`, specifically focusing on how `weeklyGoal` and `thisWeekHours` are rendered and interact with each other. I'm making sure that there are no logical errors in the displayed values.\n\n\n\n**Validating Status Logic**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the code related to the status display in `Dashboard.tsx`, focusing on the calculation of `progressPercent`, the display of `completedTopics`, and `totalTopics`. I'm validating the data sources to ensure accuracy, and I'm verifying the responsiveness of the progress bar using inline styles to the overall visual presentation of the information.\n\n\n**Refining Chart Elements**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the simulated performance chart, specifically examining the rendering of the `AreaChart` and its child elements within `Dashboard.tsx`. I'm verifying the data integration, the axes, and the use of the gradient for a clean look. I am also checking the `XAxis` and the `CartesianGrid` for data flow and consistency.\n\n\n",
