      "text": "**Envisioning the Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on the interface. It's becoming clearer: a desktop-first design, aiming for a \"website, not app\" feel with a dark theme. The aesthetic will be Dark Academia, envisioning a grand library setting with coffee and books, with a dedicated URL specified for the home page. The user wants consistent AI-generated visuals across the entire platform.\n\n\n**Refining the Aesthetics**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in the aesthetic details. The \"Midnight Scholar\" theme is taking shape: a dark academia meets high-tech hybrid look. Deep Slate with Indigo accents and glassmorphism elements will be key. I’m also implementing a \"Boss Health Bar\" style animated chart on the home page as a progress indicator, focusing on a circular Spirit Gauge with glowing effects and scanlines. I've begun making coding changes in `App.tsx` and `index.html` to reflect these updates. I am decreasing the sidebar from the w-64 size to w-56.\n\n\n**Implementing Darker Elements**\n\nI'm now making final aesthetic tweaks for the platform, focusing on a consistent dark theme. I've darkened the `.glass-card` component and incorporated keyframes for game-like animations, notably in `Dashboard.tsx`, where I’ve added a pulsing, \"Level Up\" circular progress bar. I’ve also updated grid lines to be darker and data lines to be brighter on charts. I’ve updated each component such as, `Disciplinas.tsx`, `Ciclos.tsx`, `Revisao.tsx`, `Simulados.tsx`, `Admin.tsx`, and `Profile.tsx` to utilize darker cards. I've also added Unsplash images, such as a dark library for the home page and old books for `Disciplinas`.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
