  {
    "id": 613,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Designing Confirmation Alert**\n\nI'm currently focused on implementing an intelligent confirmation alert within the `components/Disciplinas.tsx` file for topic and subject deletions. The plan is to leverage the existing obsidian-glass dark theme to ensure a seamless visual integration. I'm aiming for a user-friendly and intuitive alert design.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Implementation**\n\nI'm now shifting gears to the actual implementation. My immediate focus is on replacing the native `window.confirm` calls. I'm leaning toward a reusable `ConfirmationModal` component, although a local state-driven modal is still on the table. The aesthetic vision is solidified: obsidian glassmorphism, dark background, and high-contrast text with red/rose accents to highlight the danger. I'm aiming for a smooth fade-in effect with backdrop blur and clearly differentiated \"Confirm\" and \"Cancel\" buttons. The `confirmModal` object structure, containing the state to drive the modal with its corresponding information, is almost complete. Now I need to wrap all the delete calls with the new modal.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
