  {
    "id": 621,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Component Editing**\n\nI'm currently focused on adding edit functionality to the `Disciplinas.tsx` component. The immediate goal is to implement inline editing for both Subject and Topic names. I'm planning to use the \"Edit3\" icon from `lucide-react` as the trigger button for these edit actions. Furthermore, it's essential to preserve the existing \"Obsidian Glass\" design aesthetic throughout the modifications.\n\n\n**Implementing Edit States**\n\nI've established the state variables needed for inline editing: `editingSubjectId`, `editingTopicId`, and `tempEditValue`. Now, I'm working on how to visually represent the editable elements, differentiating between display and input modes based on these state variables within the `Disciplinas.tsx` component. For subjects, I plan to integrate the pencil icon within the subject header, while for topics, it will be placed within each topic row. I've also selected appropriate icons from `lucide-react` for edit, save/confirm, and cancel actions, and am considering a reuse of a `handleSubjectUpdate` for topic updates too.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769264784,
      "nanos": 12000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
