  {
    "id": 625,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Considering Reset Functionality**\n\nI'm currently focused on incorporating a \"clear/reset record\" feature for each topic within the 'Disciplinas' (Quests) page. The goal is to allow users to efficiently correct errors by resetting study time, dates, questions attempted, and questions answered correctly. I'm exploring the design implications and ensuring a user-friendly implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Reset Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating the reset functionality into `Disciplinas.tsx`. I've added the reset button, using the `RefreshCw` icon, and positioned it near the existing action buttons for each topic. A new `resetConfirmation` state now handles confirmation prompts before data reset, and I'm updating the `handleSubjectUpdate` logic to accommodate the reset action. My focus is on making this a clean and intuitive addition to the user experience.\n\n\n**Designing Reset Confirmation**\n\nI'm deep in the specifics of the reset functionality now. I'm focusing on the reset confirmation modal, aiming for a high-fidelity \"Obsidian Glass\" style. The amber/yellow color scheme will clearly differentiate it from the \"delete\" option. The `resetConfirmation` state is crucial, managing the confirmation workflow, and I've also implemented the visual reset button with the `RotateCcw` icon within the topic list. I'm building the `executeReset` function to make the data modifications and calling the `handleSubjectUpdate` as the final step.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
