  {
    "id": 637,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing User Registration**\n\nI'm currently focused on the user page within `components/Admin.tsx`. I've identified that new user registrations default the name to \"USUÁRIO\", and I need to address this. My immediate priority is developing a new registration flow, specifically an \"Add User\" feature. I'm also thinking through how to better represent the registered users in a more intuitive way.\n\n\n**Refining User Representation**\n\nI'm now diving into the user representation and the data to be shown. I think a sophisticated table with avatars, statuses, and icons is the way to go, keeping the \"Master UI\" look. I've also been thinking about the database side, making sure the `profiles` table is correctly structured and updated. I will add a new user modal with validation to handle the add user flow.\n\n\n**Structuring User Metadata**\n\nI've been mapping out the `profiles` table schema, detailing each field: `id`, `name`, `email`, `role`, `status`, and `last_seen`. A database trigger is also planned to handle the profile insertion/updates upon user signup via Auth. In `Admin.tsx`, I'm working to fix the \"Add User\" logic to incorporate the full name and rendering of the table. I'm also planning UX features like \"Copy Email\". Finally, I'm refactoring the user table to have a dense, clean, and informative \"Master UI\" look. My current focus is the component structure with the planned search bar, \"Add User\" button, and table/card components.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769266171,
      "nanos": 549000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
