r `isMaster`. I'm verifying the display table and that it correctly displays the intended values within the component. I'm focusing on ensuring consistency.\n\n\n**Implementing the Modal**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided modal component with the `handleAddUser` functionality within `components/Admin.tsx`, specifically focusing on the user creation process. I'm focusing on user interface consistency, incorporating error handling within the modal for a better experience.\n\n\n**Implementing the Modal**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided modal component, specifically focusing on handling the `handleAddUser` function. I'm focusing on consistency. This includes error handling within the modal. I'm prioritizing user interface clarity.\n\n\n**Integrating the Form**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided form, including email and password fields, within the new user creation modal. I'm carefully implementing the state management for `newEmail` and `newPassword`. I will ensure that the integration seamlessly handles user input and validates the values.\n\n\n**Integrating the Form**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided form, with email, password, and role fields, into the user creation modal. The state management for `newEmail`, `newPassword`, and `newRole` is being carefully implemented, ensuring user input validation. The integration handles the logic seamlessly.\n\n\n**Integrating the Form Fields**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided form, including email, password, and role fields, into the user creation modal. State management is crucial, so I'm paying careful attention to `newEmail`, `newPassword`, and `newRole` validation and integration. I'll make sure to integrate the logic seamlessly.\n\n\n**Refining Update Modal**\n\nI'm now integrating a form with name and role fields into the user update modal. I'm focusing on state management for the `newName` and `newRole` fields, to handle user input validation. The goal is seamless integration and validation.\n\n\n**Refining the Update Modal**\n\nI'm now implementing the update functionality. I've integrated a form with name and role fields into the user update modal, and I'm focusing on state management for `newName` and `newRole`. I've added user input validation.\n\n\n**Implementing the Form Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided form, including the role selection dropdown within the update modal. I'm focusing on managing the `editRole` state to ensure correct input handling and validation, and consistency with the provided code. I'm now making sure that I have correct and appropriate logic.\n\n\n**Implementing the Update Modal**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided form logic, including the role selection dropdown, within the update modal, specifically for the role selection and data validation. I'm focusing on managing the `editRole` state for correct input handling. I've ensured a smooth data flow and added appropriate logic.\n\n\n**Integrating the Edital Form**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating a form for the editais modal. I've designed the component around the existing modal, handling edital name, organization, subjects, and file uploads. I'm prioritizing data flow within the `Editais` modal, and I am making sure the logic is consistent.\n\n\n**Integrating the Edital Deletion**\n\nI'm working on integrating the `deleteEdital` functionality into the `editais` section. I've built the button that calls the delete function. I'm ensuring it functions correctly within the modal and is connected to Supabase for the `predefined_editais` table.\n\n\n**Integrating the Edital Deletion**\n\nI'm working on integrating `deleteEdital` into the `editais` section to trigger deletions for the editais table. I'm adding a button that will call the function, and it is linked to Supabase integration for the `predefined_editais` table.\n\n\n**Finalizing Edital Integration**\n\nI'm now completing the integration for the editais modal. I'm focusing on ensuring data flow for the edital name and organization within the form, so that the data updates in the `editais` table in Supabase. I'm making sure it will flow correctly.\n\n\n",
