  {
    "id": 644,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing User Management**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Admin.tsx` page, specifically the user management section. The immediate priorities are fixing the broken user deletion button and ensuring the user management page is only accessible to authorized users. I'm exploring the codebase to understand the existing logic and pinpoint the root cause of the broken functionality. Security is paramount, so access control is the top priority now.\n\n\n**Refining User Deletion**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the user deletion process within `Admin.tsx`. My focus is on implementing a confirmation modal, similar to the one in `Disciplinas.tsx`, to replace the clunky `window.confirm`. I'm also adding a crucial security guard at the start of the `Admin` component, ensuring only administrators can access this section. Furthermore, I'll review and refine `handleDeleteUser` to accurately interact with Supabase and provide appropriate feedback.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI and Security**\n\nI'm now focusing on user deletion visuals. I will prioritize the \"Intelligent Confirmation Modal\" style from `Disciplinas.tsx` for a more user-friendly experience. A \"Forbidden\" state will be added. I'll refine the `handleDeleteUser` function and debug it, as it seems the state updates may not have been triggering correctly. I'll also ensure security by checking for administrator roles. Furthermore, I will improve the \"Governanca\" UI.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
