  {
    "id": 660,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing Data Inconsistencies**\n\nI'm currently focused on resolving the problem of deleted users persisting in the Supabase database. I'm prioritizing implementing a robust cleanup mechanism to eliminate the ghost data. My design includes a multi-pronged approach, which means I'm considering both immediate deletion and archival options, along with cascade deletion implementations, which will be the first step in the clean-up. The ultimate goal is to ensure data integrity and prevent inconsistencies.\n\n\n**Refining Delete Implementation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics of the deletion process. The objective is hard deletion. I'm focusing on strengthening the session validation in `App.tsx` so that a user is signed out if their profile is deleted, as well as refining `components/Admin.tsx` to ensure the Supabase `.delete()` method is correctly utilized, handling any RLS or trigger issues. Furthermore, I will revisit the \"5 attempts\" logic in `Login.tsx`. The goal is full removal from the UI and the database.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Removal**\n\nI'm now putting the finishing touches on the user deletion implementation. I'm making sure `executeDeleteUser` in Admin.tsx targets the correct user ID with `match({ id: targetId })` and has robust error handling, alongside more informative feedback on the \"physical deletion\" process. I've also enhanced \"Locked Account\" and \"Physical Removal\" messaging in Login.tsx and ensuring the \"5 attempts\" logic is persistent. In App.tsx, I'm updating the `init` effect to strictly validate the profile and force a sign-out if the profile is null, since the auth user may still exist.\n\n\n**Improving Profile Validation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on handling null profiles after a user is deleted. I've updated the `init` effect to strictly validate the profile and force a sign-out if the user is deleted, even if the auth user still exists, fixing the issue I observed. Also, I'm making sure that the delete logic in `Admin.tsx` uses the correct target ID and has more robust error handling. I'm also ensuring the Supabase `.delete()` method correctly handles RLS or trigger issues.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
