se` and the user's role. I'll verify the generation of temporary IDs, the data insertion process, and the potential error handling. I'm focusing on the interaction between local state management and the database updates.\n\n\n**Evaluating Delete Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on `executeDelete`, and I'm analyzing how it handles both subject and topic deletions within `Disciplinas.tsx`. I'm specifically examining the logic that updates both local state (using `setSubjects`) and the remote database (using Supabase). I'm also reviewing the conditional execution based on `targetId` and its use of `startsWith('local-')` to determine whether a remote deletion should occur. I will also be looking into handling edge cases.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Save Logic**\n\nI'm now carefully analyzing the `saveTopicProgress` function within `Disciplinas.tsx`. I'm focusing on how it updates subject and topic progress, considering the time, questions, and dates. I'm verifying the data calculations and their accurate application to the relevant topic, ensuring a smooth state transition. I'm also assessing how `onAddLog` is triggered based on progress made.\n\n\n**Assessing Button Functionality**\n\nI'm now investigating the button's intended functionality within `Disciplinas.tsx`, specifically the \"CATÁLOGO MESTRE\" button. I'm focusing on the `onClick` event, which toggles the `showCatalog` state. I need to understand its role in hiding or displaying the subject catalog and ensure the logic is working as expected. I'll also check the visual state transition to make sure the icon is updated properly, and that the text is updated as well.\n\n\n**Evaluating Input Validation**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the input validation within the `addSubject` logic of `Disciplinas.tsx`. I'm going through the input field logic. I'm focusing on the `newSubjectName` state variable, and verifying that the code handles empty or invalid inputs before attempting to add a new subject. I'm focusing on preventing 