    "id": 698,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Restoring Missing Data**\n\nI'm currently focused on the frustrating absence of the Study Plan data. Despite the \"Editais\" page being restored, my subject data stubbornly remains at zero. My primary goal is to revert the system to its state on January 24, 2026, to recover my Study Plan.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Access**\n\nI'm now investigating potential access issues. My focus shifted to database-frontend synchronization. I suspect a mismatch in the `user_id`, or row-level security is causing the data blockage for my `ralysonriccelli@gmail.com` account. Specifically, I'm examining `App.tsx` and the `fetchData` function, where the `user_id` is queried in `supabase.from('subjects').select('*').eq('user_id', userId);`. Further, the `Disciplinas` component might interfere before state readiness.\n\n\n**Refining Frontend Logic**\n\nI've pinpointed an issue with `App.tsx` not re-triggering upon re-authentication. The UI shows \"MATRIZ VAZIA / SINCRONIZANDO COM O BANCO...\", meaning the fetch returns an empty array, not null. I need to widen the frontend query for my master user, checking for email-based data (legacy data). A \"Data Recovery\" mode is crucial, using fallback keys if UUID fails. Also, better UI feedback to distinguish between empty databases and ongoing searches is necessary. Finally, I'll refine `App.tsx` to prevent unintended data clearing.\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Retrieval**\n\nI'm now implementing more robust error handling and data retrieval. I'm focusing on `App.tsx` and have refactored `fetchData` to be more resilient, especially for the master user, preventing premature terminations when subData is empty. Additionally, I'm ensuring optimal client configuration in `lib/supabase.ts`. I also improved the placeholder logic in `Disciplinas.tsx` to be more reassuring during syncing. I will introduce a fallback mechanism in `fetchData` that uses the email in a metadata field if the UUID link is broken.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
