      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Investigating Missing Data**\n\nI'm currently troubled by the missing data from the 6 PM study. It seemed saved, but now it's vanished! I'm logged in, but there are no subjects or disciplines appearing. I'm also pondering the function of a particular field, and what that might have to do with the disappeared data.\n\n\n**Tracing Data Discrepancies**\n\nI'm now focusing on discrepancies. It appears Ralyson's data is fragmented across various user IDs, including `...844`, `...8e1`, `...72b`, and `...0d4`, despite him being logged in under `...844`. His 'master sync' should gather data tied to `ralysonriccelli@gmail.com`. I'm especially perplexed by how he saw data at 18:00 if the last subject entry was at 12:58. If it wasn't there, where was it?\n\n\n**Clarifying User Session Anomalies**\n\nI'm now investigating the potential causes for the missing data entries. I am leaning toward the user either using a local session or experiencing a silent sync failure. I'm noting the `study_logs` screenshot indicates a user ID ending in `...8e1`. I am considering the purpose of `study_logs`, which tracks session data for generating charts, versus `subjects` which stores accumulated time. I am now focused on possible explanations for the 18:00 edits not appearing if the screenshot has the last update at 12:58. This could be data saved in another table, or Supabase project. It could also be saved under a different user ID, or never reached the database.\n\n\n**Reconciling Data Sources**\n\nMy focus is now on the `study_logs` data and the 18:00 discrepancy. I'm considering aggressive syncing and refining `App.tsx` to retrieve all Ralyson's data across IDs. I'll implement a \"Debug Mode\" to expose all associated IDs. I now see the 18:00 data is either using an unknown ID, or hidden by RLS policies. It's odd the \"subjects\" screenshot ends at 12:58.\n\n\n**Confirming Updated Records**\n\nI'm now thinking the user might have updated existing records. This would explain the `created_at` timestamp. I'm focusing on the `topics` column (JSONB) to confirm the new data is there. I'm noting the user's ID ending in `...8e1` in `study_logs`, and they are currently logged in as `...844`. I'll introduce a \"Deep Search\" to link all entries under a single view. The user will be reassured by \"Sincronização Multi-ID Ativa.\" I will focus on updating fetching logic in `App.tsx` and adding a \"Recovery Status\" indicator. I'm also ensuring clarity on the role of `study_logs`.\n\n\n",
