    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing User Data Flow**\n\nOkay, I'm now looking at Ralyson, specifically how his edits to \"Língua Inglesa\" as `estudante@gmail.com` are not showing up in the `study_logs`. The issue seems to be centered around disconnected user identities (UUIDs) across different tests. It feels like the data flow is broken or that some mapping isn't happening correctly. This disconnection is frustrating, and it is my primary focus now.\n\n\n**Clarifying Log Creation**\n\nI realize now that edits to topic titles don't generate study logs; logs come from recorded study sessions. My focus shifts to pinpointing how user-specific edits are isolated. The \"Master-Sync\" logic seems irrelevant. I'm checking `Disciplinas.tsx` and `handleSubjectUpdate`, but the issue appears to stem from a disconnect in perception vs. action – an edit isn't a study session, so there is no log by design. I'm clarifying this for data integrity.\n\n\n**Enforcing User Data Isolation**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing strict `user_id` filtering across the application to enforce the \"each user sees only their own data\" rule. The \"Master Fusion\" logic is removed, and I must explain why other account data is no longer accessible from the main account. I will ensure `saveTopicProgress` accurately reflects in `study_logs` and make the distinction between subject update vs. study session clear. Also, the \"REGISTRAR SESSÃO\" flow must work flawlessly. The dashboard must accurately represent data.\n\n\n",
