    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Confirming Data Persistence**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing a quick visual notification, likely a toast or alert, on the `Disciplinas` (Quests) page. The goal is to provide immediate feedback to the user whenever data, including date, time, and questions, is successfully written to the `study_logs` table. This should create a more user-friendly experience by visually confirming data persistence.\n\n\n**Implementing Success Toast**\n\nI've made progress on the success toast implementation. I've added local state (`showSuccessToast`) and a `useEffect` hook for auto-hiding. Inside `saveTopicProgress`, I'm setting `showSuccessToast(true)` upon successful Supabase insert. I'm also planning the toast's visual design: fixed bottom-right, indigo/emerald glow, blur background, and subtle animations, with an icon, \"Synchronized\" status, and a brief message. Now I am carefully reviewing `components/Disciplinas.tsx` to integrate these changes efficiently.\n\n\n**Refining Toast Integration**\n\nI've realized the code already has `showSuccessToast` and its JSX defined, so now I am focusing on refining its existing implementation in `components/Disciplinas.tsx`. My current focus is ensuring the toast is visually prominent, fully integrated, and accurately reflects successful data persistence within the application. I'll re-read the prompt and make adjustments to the logic and visual appearance as needed to fulfill the user's intent.\n\n\n**Optimizing Toast Appearance**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the success toast's visual details. Specifically, I'm working to make it stand out more effectively on the screen. The existing code uses a `div` element with specific styling, and I will be working with the code to ensure it's visually prominent while also fitting the application's overall design aesthetic. I'm also ensuring the message is clear, concise, and easy for the user to understand at a glance.\n\n\n**Enhancing Toast Details**\n\nI'm now refining the `showSuccessToast` component. I will be incorporating a progress bar to show the user when it will disappear. I'll also add details like minutes and number of questions to the success message. My focus is now on ensuring a smooth animation. Also, I'm updating `saveTopicProgress`.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
