  {
    "id": 743,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Saving Logic**\n\nI'm currently focused on the saving behavior for the `Disciplinas` page, particularly the study log. It seems the current implementation only saves data if study time (`totalMins`) is positive. My next task is to re-evaluate this condition to include cases where the user inputs a date, questions, or score, ensuring these are also recorded in `study_logs`. This will necessitate an adjustment to the saving logic.\n\n\n**Adjusting Save Triggers**\n\nI'm now revising the save trigger in `saveTopicProgress`. The aim is to log entries in `study_logs` when *any* meaningful data is provided, not just positive study time. The saving condition is being modified to include dates, questions/scores, or study time. The `minutes` field in the schema is also being considered; a zero value should still allow a save to register a session. Finally, I'm working on customizing the toast notification to indicate the nature of what's saved.\n\n\n**Implementing Zero-Time Saves**\n\nI'm now implementing the saving of study sessions even when the time is zero, specifically in `saveTopicProgress`. The goal is to ensure all user actions are recorded. I'll modify the `saveTopicProgress` function to accommodate this, as per my decision. The `minutes` column in `study_logs` will be set to zero if time isn't provided. Additionally, I'll need to confirm that `study_logs` correctly records all intended data.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769295619,
      "nanos": 155000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769295645,
      "nanos": 634000000
    }
