  {
    "id": 751,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing the Reset Bug**\n\nI'm focusing on the \"Reset\" button issue in `Disciplinas.tsx`. It appears the topic progress reset isn't functioning correctly – likely a logic or UI problem. My current task is to add an alert to confirm the reset action when the user clicks the button, improving usability.\n\n\n**Refining the Reset Logic**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the actual \"Reset\" functionality within `Disciplinas.tsx`. My previous focus on an alert seems secondary; the user is experiencing a bug. I need to ensure it clears the progress data, specifically `studyTimeMinutes`, `questionsAttempted`, `questionsCorrect`, and `lastStudiedAt`. I'll adapt my existing `deleteConfirmation` state logic to ensure the reset action is triggered properly and consistently with the UI.\n\n\n**Implementing a Custom Modal**\n\nI'm moving forward with a custom modal alert for the reset action in `Disciplinas.tsx`. I've decided against `window.confirm`. I plan to integrate the modal alert, using the same style as previous confirmations, to enhance the UI/UX. Currently, I'm adapting the state management; I will change `deleteConfirmation` to `activeModal` to accommodate different types of confirmations. This way, I can trigger the \"Reset Alert\" from `handleResetTopic` and dynamically render the appropriate buttons within the modal based on the confirmation type. I will also have `actionConfirmation` to keep it clean.\n\n\n**Validating the Reset Action**\n\nI'm now integrating the modal confirmation for the reset action within `Disciplinas.tsx`. I'm also ensuring the reset logic fully aligns with the latest data validation. I've re-examined `handleResetTopic` and confirmed it updates the subject correctly. I'm focusing on the reset action and the modal; my priority now is on adapting the UI to show the styled modal/alert and integrate the `handleResetTopic` function.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
