  {
    "id": 755,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Component Features**\n\nI'm currently focused on expanding the \"Quick Look\" feature within the `Disciplinas.tsx` component. The plan involves incorporating key performance indicators: time spent, date, number of questions attempted, correct answers, and overall efficiency percentage. Furthermore, I'm thinking about implementing a color-coding system to visually represent efficiency levels.\n\n\n**Implementing Efficiency Coloring**\n\nI've got the color-coding for efficiency levels defined: green for 80%+, orange for 60-79.99%, and red for below 60%. I'm working on the color logic and class application now. The efficiency calculation is straightforward: (corrects / total) * 100. Also, I'm integrating this color scheme into the \"Quick Look\" view while keeping the cyberpunk UI vibe. I'm extracting the necessary data points.\n\n\n**Refining \"Quick Look\" Display**\n\nI've added the calendar icon and date display, formatted in Brazilian Portuguese, to the \"Quick Look\" feature, handling potential null/undefined values. The \"Acertos / Total\" ratio is now explicit, and I've updated the color logic to green (80%+), amber (60-79.99%), and red (below 60%). I'm ensuring everything is responsive, too. I'm focusing on the date, number of questions, and acertos/total information.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
