    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Adding Test Date Countdown**\n\nI'm currently focused on incorporating a test date registration into the edital/disciplinas page. The plan is to include a dynamic countdown card on the dashboard, utilizing the test date data imported from the edital. I'm taking on this task as a Senior Full Stack Dev & Web Designer, working towards implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Exam Date Integration**\n\nI'm now focusing on how to best integrate the exam date registration. I've realized that the `examDate` exists in `PredefinedEdital` but not directly in the `Subject` type. My initial thought is to store the date when the user imports an edital. I'm considering associating the exam date with the user's current study goal or the `StudyCycle` object on the dashboard, which receives `cycle` and the `StudyCycle` does have an `examDate`. I'm leaning towards adding a user-settable \"Exam Date\" within `Disciplinas.tsx` to reflect on the dashboard.\n\n\n**Implementing Exam Date Tracking**\n\nI'm now diving into the implementation. I plan to add an exam date input to `Disciplinas.tsx`, letting users configure their test date. This date will be persisted, and I'm currently deciding between several options: the `profiles` table, a dedicated metadata field, or even `localStorage`. Next, I'll update `App.tsx` to manage the `userExamDate` state. Finally, I'll design and integrate a \"Countdown Card\" into `Dashboard.tsx`, aiming for a visually appealing, high-tech design. I have to see how to incorporate `exam_date` into the `User` object, or whether to create a general user preference.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Persistence Design**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on data persistence. I'll add `examDate?: string` to `User` within `types.ts`, and I'll manage `user.examDate` in `App.tsx`. I'll update the user profile in Supabase whenever the date is modified. I'll also add a UI element to `Disciplinas.tsx` allowing for setting the test date. The dashboard countdown will then be calculated from the stored date.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
