      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Focusing Dashboard Design**\n\nI'm currently concentrating on the dashboard (\"inicio\") page, specifically the \"Contagem Regressiva\" (Countdown) card. My priority is ensuring this card's size aligns perfectly with the existing stat cards like \"Tempo Bruto\" and \"Ritmo Semanal.\" I'm working to achieve visual consistency across the dashboard elements.\n\n\n**Addressing Date Bug and Layout**\n\nI'm now tackling the date discrepancy, identifying it stems from timezone handling when converting the date string. To fix it in `Dashboard.tsx`, I'll adjust the date conversion method. I'm also analyzing the card size issue on the Dashboard, aiming to unify the countdown card dimensions with the stat cards. This requires potentially moving the \"Trilha da Nomeação\" card or redesigning the layout, since the countdown card is currently placed in a grid-spanning section.\n\n\n**Refining Dashboard Grid**\n\nI'm now implementing the layout changes. I've decided to append `T12:00:00` or treat the date as local to fix the timezone issue. In `Dashboard.tsx`, I'll move the Countdown card to the stat cards row and adjust the \"Trilha da Nomeação\" to span the full top row. The stat cards row will go from four to five columns to incorporate the Countdown card. I am ensuring that the countdown card styling matches the existing stat cards for visual consistency, like padding and fonts.\n\n\n**Optimizing Dashboard Display**\n\nI'm now refining the dashboard grid, confirming the move of the countdown card and adjusting column spans. I'm ensuring the \"Trilha da Nomeação\" card now spans three columns in the top row. I'm also adding the countdown card to the stat cards row. To handle the date discrepancy, I'm appending 'T12:00:00' to the exam date string to calculate the `target`. I'll also ensure that the layout is responsive, and that all cards are uniform.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
