    "id": 782,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing User Management**\n\nI'm currently focused on the User Management page, specifically Admin.tsx. My immediate task is to address the reported issue with the user deletion button – it's broken. I'll need to debug it and implement a proper fix. Concurrently, I'll be adding a crucial confirmation prompt to prevent accidental deletions.\n\n\n**Refining Deletion Logic**\n\nI'm now deep-diving into the user deletion function within Admin.tsx. While Supabase's cascade might seem sufficient, the requirement for complete database cleanup necessitates a more robust solution. I will implement a sequential deletion within the `handleDeleteUser` to ensure all related records (subjects, logs, etc.) are purged before the user profile is removed. This approach prioritizes database integrity and addresses the user's optimization request.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Purge**\n\nI'm now implementing the full data purge for user deletion in `Admin.tsx`. My current focus is refining the `handleDeleteUser` function. I've incorporated a prominent \"Hard Delete\" confirmation modal with visual warnings. I'm ensuring all dependent data in `study_logs`, `mocks`, `study_cycles`, `subjects`, and `profiles` are deleted sequentially or using `Promise.all` to maintain database integrity and user experience.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
