      "text": "**Fixing User Management Page**\n\nI'm currently focused on the user management page, specifically Admin.tsx. My immediate goal is to repair the broken delete button. I need to implement a warning modal before deletion to prevent accidental data loss. The requirement is physical deletion of users and all associated information.\n\n\n**Addressing Database Integrity**\n\nI've been examining the database integrity after a user deletion, focusing on ensuring all associated records are also removed. The error log and user feedback point to orphaned records in the database, specifically concerning foreign key constraints. I'm focusing on modifying the database deletion logic in Admin.tsx. I am preparing to implement 'ON DELETE CASCADE' in the database, and double-checking that deletion is correctly implemented, so that any record deletion is atomic.\n\n\n**Refining User Deletion**\n\nI'm now refining the user deletion process in Admin.tsx to incorporate a purge protocol. This involves a warning modal with explicit destruction warnings. I'm focusing on ensuring the code correctly calls the Supabase client for deletion and accurately updates the UI state after the operation. I'm verifying the physical deletion process, making sure all associated data is cleaned up properly. I am mindful that I must only provide the code for deletion, not execute any SQL directly.\n\n\n**Restoring List View & Protocol**\n\nI'm now focused on restoring the detailed list view in `Admin.tsx`, including Name, Email, Status, Level, and Connectivity information. I will then implement the \"Purge Protocol\" modal for user deletion, with visual style refinements. The goal is to ensure `handlePurgeUser` correctly deletes the record from Supabase. I'm also incorporating role badges, status badges (Active, Suspended, Blocked), and a connectivity LED (Online/Offline) for a clearer visual representation.\n\n\n",
