      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Fixing the Deletion Function**\n\nI'm focusing on the user deletion function. Right now, it's broken, so I'm adding a confirmation warning to prevent accidental deletions. The most important update is that I'm implementing a \"hard delete\" to physically remove all associated records from the database. This ensures complete data integrity.\n\n\n**Addressing Database Optimization**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on database optimization, specifically tackling a foreign key constraint violation. The `subjects` table is giving me grief; it seems there's \"garbage\" data with a `user_id` that doesn't exist in the `profiles` table. My current focus is to clean up these orphaned entries before implementing the `ON DELETE CASCADE` constraint. I'll need to do some cleaning up first.\n\n\n**Refining the UI/UX**\n\nI'm making headway on the UI, specifically for the \"War Room\" warning. My focus is on making the `handlePurgeUser` function robust. I'll provide an updated `Admin.tsx`, along with the SQL script for cleaning and optimizing the database. I'm clarifying why the error occurred, which was due to orphaned data during the `ALTER TABLE` process, and how to fix this by deleting the orphans. I will fix the delete button, so it is operational, and also updates locally.\n\n\n",
