    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Investigating Deletion Issue**\n\nI'm currently looking into a data integrity problem. A user deletion action on the frontend is not cascading as expected to the `profiles` table in Supabase. I've also identified a related foreign key constraint violation on the `subjects` table, suggesting further potential inconsistencies. I will explore the database triggers or application logic to understand the cause and implement a fix.\n\n\n**Confirming Data Integrity Error**\n\nI've confirmed a data integrity problem due to a foreign key violation. Specifically, the error code 23503 indicates orphaned records in the `subjects` table, meaning some `user_id` values exist there that are absent in the `profiles` table. The user provided an image showing the data and confirmed `4fb46263...` is missing from `profiles`, so it is definitely orphaned. The SQL fix failed initially, so I must remove the orphaned records, likely in several steps. My immediate focus is to perform SQL cleanup and remove orphaned records from all child tables, before applying any `ON DELETE CASCADE` fixes.\n\n\n**Refining Purge Implementation**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing the \"Purge\" functionality within the UI, starting with updates to `Admin.tsx`. My strategy involves a hard delete from the `profiles` table using the Supabase client. This action will trigger the database cascade, but I'll make sure to clean up all orphans first using a comprehensive SQL script. I'm refining the modal dialog with technical details and improving the admin table display. I am updating `handlePurgeUser` to use `supabase.from('profiles').delete()`.\n\n\n",
