    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Fixing the \"Editais\" Display**\n\nI'm tackling a critical bug on the \"Editais\" page. The issue is clear: data isn't rendering from the `predefined_editais` table in the Admin component. My focus is on diagnosing the data flow.\n\n\n**Rendering the `editais` Data**\n\nI've identified the root cause: the \"Editais\" view in `Admin.tsx` uses a placeholder, ignoring the passed `editais` data. The data flows correctly from `App.tsx` via the `editais` prop. I'm focusing on replacing the placeholder with a proper data display—likely a table or list.\n\n\n**Enhancing \"Editais\" Functionality**\n\nI'm now expanding the \"Editais\" feature set. This involves enabling edital deletion and addition/editing capabilities within the admin interface. I'm prioritizing the creation of a visual design that aligns with the established \"High-Tech/Master UI\" theme, implementing dark, translucent cards with indigo accents, bold typography, and status badges. I'm focusing on the component that renders the list of editais, including adding delete buttons with confirmation.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
