  {
    "id": 824,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Fixing Admin Page Bugs**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Admin.tsx` page. The \"Edit\" and \"Delete\" buttons within the editais list are non-functional, as is the \"New Matrix\" button. My priority is to address these bugs, ensuring the functionality of these key UI elements. Throughout this process, I will ensure that the UI/UX maintains its high quality.\n\n\n**Addressing Edital Functions**\n\nI've made progress on the \"Delete\" functionality. Although the modal is present and `handleDeleteEdital` is defined, I will double-check that the deletion is executed correctly within the modal and that it works properly. Also, I've outlined plans to implement an \"Edit\" function, tracking the edital being modified. For the \"New Matrix\" button, I've begun planning an entry modal for initial data, with the ultimate goal of having a full form or skeleton builder for new editais.\n\n\n**Verifying Security and Logic**\n\nI'm now diving into the deletion process, which looks fairly solid from an initial assessment. I'm focusing on confirming the use of Role-Level Security (RLS) and double-checking the Supabase call for correctness and data integrity. I'm also reviewing user permissions to ensure that only administrators can perform these actions. I have an outline for a modal, state, and form handling for both edit and create actions.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769302844,
      "nanos": 416000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769302853,
      "nanos": 650000000
    }
