orrectly setting the `editalToDelete` state, as well as the triggering of the modal.\n\n\n**Validating Date Formatting**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the date formatting within the edital cards, ensuring the `examDate` displays correctly. I'm checking to make sure it handles null or undefined values and displays a default value if it's missing. I am checking it is in a readable format.\n\n\n\n**Validating Empty State**\n\nI'm now making sure that the empty state message for editais displays correctly when there are no results. I'm scrutinizing the conditional rendering based on the `filteredEditais.length` and ensuring the appropriate message is shown when the database is empty, and the UI responds as expected.\n\n\n\n**Validating Input Field Connections**\n\nI'm now investigating the connection of input fields to their respective state variables within the edital edit form. I'm confirming that the `nome_do_concurso` input and other relevant fields are correctly bound to their corresponding state values, ensuring changes in the input fields update the state appropriately and vice-versa.\n\n\n**Validating Form State Updates**\n\nI'm now focusing on the edital edit form. I am checking to make sure the input fields for 'name' and 'organization' are correctly updating the state variables `editalForm.name` and `editalForm.organization` using the `onChange` handler, and that the state updates are correctly applied. I will verify that `setEditalForm` is functioning as intended.\n\n\n**Verifying Date Input Binding**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the exam date input field within the `editalForm`. I'm confirming that the `examDate` value is correctly updated by the `onChange` handler, utilizing the spread operator for state updates. Also, I will check the connection between the input's `value` attribute and `editalForm.examDate`.\n\n\n\n**Validating Delete Interaction**\n\nI'm now deep-diving into the delete confirmation modal and the `handleDeleteEdital` function. I'm carefully examining the conditional rendering of the modal, the `onClick` handler of the delete button, and the state updates related to `editalToDelete`. I'm verifying the data flow and actions, making sure the process is smooth and consistent.\n\n\n**Refining Card Button Interactions**\n\nI've added `e.stopPropagation()` and specified `type=\"button\"` to the card buttons. I've also implemented `pointer-events-none` on the background icon and put the actions in a container with `relative z-10`. These changes ensure reliable and correct button interaction with the admin interface.\n\n\n**Streamlining Deletion & Parsing**\n\nI've simplified the `handleDeleteEdital` function to streamline deletion by reading `editalToDelete` directly. I've also added a type check to `refreshData`, handling the JSON string from the Supabase subjects field. I've also improved the UX by updating the action button hovers.\n\n\n",
