    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Core Editais Buttons**\n\nI'm currently focused on the \"Core Editais\" section within the `Admin.tsx` component. The user wants me to address the edit and delete buttons. I've started examining the code responsible for rendering the 'editais' cards, particularly the JSX defining those buttons, to figure out what needs to be changed and in what ways. The goal is to correct any issues with the edit and delete functionalities.\n\n\n**Re-Examining Button Logic**\n\nI've re-examined the click handlers for both the edit and delete buttons within the `Admin.tsx` file, specifically within the Core Editais section. The handlers *are* present, so I'm investigating the associated logic to figure out why they're not functioning as expected. I'm focusing on `handleOpenEditalModal` and how it sets state for editing, specifically to identify what may be breaking the connection to the modal.\n\n\n**Investigating Event Propagation**\n\nI've confirmed `handleOpenEditalModal` appears correct in setting the editing state and opening the modal. I suspect an issue with event propagation now, as the logic itself seems sound, particularly in the `Admin.tsx` file. Regarding the delete button, I'm examining how `editalToDelete` is used to render the deletion modal. I'm focusing on the click handlers.\n\n\n**Diagnosing UI Overlap**\n\nI've determined `handleDeleteEdital` calls Supabase as expected. However, the reported malfunction prompts a UI-focused investigation. I suspect the issue could be an overlapping element, specifically the `Database` icon in the background, set with `absolute` positioning. Its `opacity-5` is likely obscuring the buttons, as they're within a container positioned after the icon in the DOM with a relative parent. I'll need to verify z-index or container size to confirm. I've started examining the `PredefinedEdital` type for related details.\n\n\n**Confirming Click Handlers**\n\nI've been re-examining the `Admin.tsx` code, specifically the button click handlers. I've noted the `edital` prop passed to both `handleOpenEditalModal` and `setEditalToDelete`, confirming the correct edit and delete data are bound. I also see the card's grouping and icon styling, and I believe the click-through issue is due to the parent card's `group` class and the icon's `group-hover:opacity-10`, as they may prevent the button clicks from registering. I'll verify the z-index to confirm. Finally, I noticed the `id` from Supabase is being converted to a `string`, which should be fine.\n\n\n**Verifying Element Visibility**\n\nI'm now focusing on the visibility issue with the delete button, prompted by my confusion over the non-functionality of the edit and delete buttons. I've re-examined the decorative icon's positioning and styling. Specifically, the element's positioning with `absolute top-0 right-0` leads me to believe it overlaps the buttons, obscuring their click events. I'll add `pointer-events-none` to the icon to test this theory. To be safe, I will apply `relative z-10` to the buttons. Additionally, I need to check the `handleDeleteEdital` function.\n\n\n**Refining Button Interactivity**\n\nI've been meticulously reviewing the `Admin.tsx` file and identified improvements to refine button interactivity. I'll be adding `z-10` and `relative` to the button container, and `pointer-events-none` to the decorative icon, to clarify click events, specifically in relation to the edit and delete buttons. I'll also check the scope of the `handleOpenEditalModal` and `handleDeleteEdital` functions. Finally, I will ensure the modals are rendered properly and confirm the logic surrounding `edital.id`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Component Re-Render**\n\nI'm now considering the re-rendering of the entire component, `Admin.tsx`, related to the edit and delete buttons. The updates to the `editais` state happen within `App.tsx` and are passed as a prop, which likely triggers a full re-render, even if only part of the data changes. I need to consider an alternative implementation or optimization. I'm focusing on ensuring changes to the data properly reflect in the UI.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Fixes**\n\nMy analysis indicates the decorative `Database` icon, positioned absolutely, is likely overlapping and obstructing the click events of the edit and delete buttons. To resolve this, I'll add `pointer-events-none` to the icon's container. I'm also adding `relative z-20` to the button container to guarantee they are on top. I will also incorporate `e.stopPropagation()` in case of any event propagation issues. I'll focus on testing the effects of these updates.\n\n\n**Applying UI/UX Enhancements**\n\nI'm now implementing the UI/UX changes. I'll add `pointer-events-none` to the background icon container and apply `relative z-20` to the action buttons container within the `Edital` card component. I will also check the state updates and the modals themselves, confirming the `handleOpenEditalModal` correctly sets the edit form data, as well as the delete handler.\n\n\n",
