    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Dashboard Edits**\n\nI'm currently focused on the `Dashboard.tsx` component, specifically the \"página inicial\". The task involves adjusting the \"tempo bruto\" card. I plan to change its displayed text to \"tempo de estudo\" and verify that the count within the card accurately reflects all study time entries for the user. I believe the implementation is correct, but I'll ensure full consistency.\n\n\n**Revising Time Calculations**\n\nI'm now diving deeper into the time calculations, specifically within `Dashboard.tsx`. I was using `subjects` to compute `totalMinutes`, however the user specified that \"all time records\" must be counted. The \"totalHours\" calculation, which is currently reliant on `subjects.topics.studyTimeMinutes`, needs refinement. I'm leaning toward using `studyLogs` instead, as this is the source of truth for all records. I'm focusing on ensuring data accuracy. Furthermore, I'll proceed with removing the \"media simulados\" card, changing the \"meta\" card text to \"meta semanal\", and removing the \"ritmo semanal\" card.\n\n\n**Calculating Absolute Time**\n\nI've got the absolute total time calculated using `studyLogs`, which I'm confident is the correct source. I've built `absoluteTotalMinutes` and `absoluteTotalHours` using `useMemo` for efficiency. Now, I'm focusing on updating the card labels (\"tempo bruto\" to \"tempo de estudo\", and \"meta\" to \"meta semanal\") and removing the \"media simulados\" and \"ritmo semanal\" cards. I'll need to adapt the grid layout (`grid-cols`) in `Dashboard.tsx` to accommodate the change from five cards to three.\n\n\n**Adjusting Study Time Display**\n\nI've finalized the study time calculations using `studyLogs` which accurately reflects \"todos os registros\". The `Dashboard.tsx` component is my current focus, I'm now implementing the label changes and card removals. I've switched the text on the \"tempo bruto\" card to \"tempo de estudo\", and the \"meta\" card to \"meta semanal\", and removed \"media simulados\". I'm rethinking the grid layout, and I think `md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-3` is a good layout for the three remaining cards.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
