    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Revising Dashboard Design**\n\nI'm currently focused on the dashboard's design consistency. Specifically, I'm working to integrate the \"Dias p/ prova\" card's visual style with \"Tempo de Estudo\" and \"Meta Semanal\" for a cohesive look. In addition, I'm adding a new \"Questões\" card to provide a summary of questions attempted.\n\n\n**Calculating Overall Progress**\n\nI've been calculating the \"Aproveitamento\" card, my new focus. It will show the total percentage of correct answers. I'm pulling data from the topics and mock exams. For the \"Questões\" card, I'm summing `questionsAttempted` from topics and `totalQuestions` from mocks. Then, for the \"Aproveitamento\" card, I am going to sum the `questionsCorrect` from topics and `score` from mocks.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Integration**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating the unique \"Dias p/ prova\" card while maintaining its functionality, such as the edit button and color variations when the test is close. My aim is to align its border style, padding, and icons with the other cards, and to update the grid to accommodate five columns. I have checked the user's logic for calculating `totalStudyMinutes`, and the current code is correct.\n\n\n**Finalizing Card Metrics**\n\nI'm now implementing the `useMemo` hook to calculate question statistics efficiently, pulling data from both subjects/topics and mocks. I'm utilizing the `Target` icon for the \"Questões\" card and `Trophy` or `Activity` for \"Aproveitamento.\" I'm ensuring the \"Dias p/ Prova\" edit button maintains alignment. The color coding (green/red) is planned for the \"Aproveitamento\" card, and I'll confirm the `Edit2` button integration.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
