      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing Code Differences**\n\nI'm currently focused on the proposed code change for `Ciclos.tsx`. I see that the user's snippet uses `CycleSubject` and `Ciclo` imports, which need careful comparison against `types.ts`. I want to ensure these imports align correctly with the existing structure and definitions. There are some concerns about potential inconsistencies which are worth further investigation before any changes are made.\n\n\n**Addressing Dependencies**\n\nI've determined that the user's code relies on several undefined types and functions. Specifically, `StudyCycle`, `NivelConhecimento`, `PesoDisciplina`, `CycleSubject`, and `Ciclo` are missing from `types.ts`, and `calcularTempoEstudo` and `gerarCiclos` are unavailable. My immediate plan is to update `types.ts` to include the necessary interfaces and enums to avoid breaking the code. I'll need to carefully define these elements based on how they're used in the provided code snippets.\n\n\n**Defining New Types**\n\nI'm now focused on fleshing out `types.ts`. I've added the `NivelConhecimento` and `PesoDisciplina` enums, along with the `CycleSubject` interface, which extends `Subject` and includes knowledge level, discipline weight, and study time. I've also defined the `Ciclo` interface, which includes the list of subjects and total study time, and the relevant `StudyCycle` interface. Next, I plan to move on to the service functions.\n\n\n**Refining Type Definitions**\n\nI'm now refining the `StudyCycle` update in `types.ts` to ensure compatibility and functionality. I plan to incorporate the new fields into the `StudyCycle` interface, including the exam date, hours per day, schedule, and the new configuration properties. I'll include `config_disciplinas`, `disciplinas_por_ciclo`, `meta_atual`, `ciclo_atual`, `metas_concluidas`, and `materias_concluidas_ids` to the type definitions. Concurrently, I'll be working on creating `services/cycleLogic.ts` and updating `Ciclos.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Cycle Logic**\n\nI've created `services/cycleLogic.ts` and defined `calcularTempoEstudo` and `gerarCiclos`. The `calcularTempoEstudo` function calculates study time based on knowledge level and discipline weight, while `gerarCiclos` generates study cycles, distributing subjects evenly across four cycles using a rotating slice. Next, I plan to integrate these functions into my `Ciclos.tsx` file to get the overall functionality working as intended.\n\n\n**Verifying Data Structures**\n\nI'm now investigating potential discrepancies between the new `StudyCycle` structure and the Supabase table `study_cycles`. My immediate concern is that the existing `database_fix.sql` script does not seem to include the relevant changes. I need to ensure the data fetching logic in `App.tsx` and the `StudyCycle` type definition in `types.ts` are synchronized. The TS compiler will throw errors if I don't address this. The user's goal is to update the site with this logic.\n\n\n**Integrating New Functions**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating `calcularTempoEstudo` and `gerarCiclos` into `Ciclos.tsx`, after making sure I update those functions into my codebase. I see that the new `StudyCycle` in `Ciclos.tsx` expects fields like `config_disciplinas`, `disciplinas_por_ciclo`, and others. I'll need to define how the data is handled.\n\n\n**Confirming Data Integrity**\n\nI'm now cross-referencing the `StudyCycle` interface with the user's `Ciclos.tsx` snippet and my own code. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency between the types and the expected data structure, particularly around `config_disciplinas`, `disciplinas_por_ciclo`, and the service functions. I'll need to double check the Postgres casing of the fields. I'm also confirming the import path for `calcularTempoEstudo` and `gerarCiclos`, to ensure smooth integration.\n\n\n",
