    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Defining Cycle State Storage**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the database storage for the \"Ciclos\" (Cycles) page. Specifically, I need to save the study plan cycle state in Supabase, including subject completion marks within each phase. I'm prioritizing storing which subjects are completed/not completed and capturing completion events.\n\n\n**Refining Completion Logic**\n\nI'm now refining how I handle phase advancement and subject completion. I need to ensure the `handleToggleMateria` function correctly updates the `materias_concluidas_ids` array and triggers the `saveCycleState` function. I'm focusing on ensuring data consistency between the UI and database when marking subjects done or undone, and that the data is saved, so I'm testing the logic in `components/Ciclos.tsx`. The increments to `ciclo_atual` are a concern for phase advancement, and need to be consistent with marking things as done or not.\n\n\n**Synchronizing UI and Database**\n\nI'm now focusing on synchronizing the UI and database after cycle completion. I need to make sure `saveCycleState` updates the React state with the database response. I'll add a loading indicator for better UX feedback on \"Toggle\" and \"Complete\" actions. I'm verifying the data persistence for subject markings within phases and cycle completion; the \"gerar e salvar planilha\" button is working, so now I am focusing on these other actions.\n\n\n**Implementing Real-time Sync**\n\nI'm now implementing real-time synchronization between the UI and the database by making `handleToggleMateria` and `handleCompleteCycle` asynchronous to ensure immediate database updates. I'm adding a \"Saving\" status indicator to provide real-time feedback. I've verified the `materias_concluidas_ids` column mapping in the payload, but I'm concerned about the `instanceId` generation in `services/cycleLogic.ts`, since `Date.now()` causes it to change on rerenders. I will solve this issue immediately.\n\n\n**Fixing Instance ID Instability**\n\nI'm making the `instanceId` deterministic to prevent inconsistencies when regenerating cycles, aiming for stability when saving only IDs. I'm focusing on ensuring it remains consistent across cycle generations. I'm modifying `services/cycleLogic.ts` to generate `instanceId` deterministically and updating `components/Ciclos.tsx` for real-time syncing. I'm also reviewing database table structures based on user feedback to align with the current implementation.\n\n\n",
