    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Envisioning Edit Functionality**\n\nI'm focusing on the \"undo\" functionality within the study planning platform. The primary goal is to empower users to revise completed phases or subjects, which would enable editing the subject matter or cycle in which they exist. The current constraints involve leveraging the capabilities of a senior fullstack developer and web designer. I'm brainstorming the most elegant yet robust implementation for this feature.\n\n\n**Implementing Undo Actions**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specific code modifications required within `Ciclos.tsx`. My current focus is integrating three distinct undo mechanisms. First, individual subject unchecking needs to be refined for user-friendliness. Second, a \"Return to Previous Phase\" button will allow for phase rollbacks. Finally, a reset option for the current state. The 'Rollback' icon placement and styling are also on my mind, while ensuring robust Supabase state updates. If the current cycle is greater than 1, decrement it.\n\n\n**Refining Rollback Logic**\n\nI'm now deep-diving into the edge case handling for phase rollbacks, particularly when `ciclo_atual` is 1. If `ciclo_atual` is 1, and the current meta (phase) is greater than 1, I need to decrease the `meta_atual`, set `ciclo_atual` to 4, and decrement `metas_concluidas`. I've decided to clear `materias_concluidas_ids` on phase rollback to provide a clean slate. I'm focusing on implementing a `handleRollbackPhase` function within `Ciclos.tsx`, complete with a UI button and confirmation. Visual feedback is key. I'll need to remember to allow the edit request, or at least, notify the user that an edit may be requested on their study cycle.\n\n\n",
