  {
    "id": 902,
    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Refining Completion Logic**\n\nI've been focusing on the \"Ciclos\" page and how to manage phase completion. My current approach involves automatically unmarking a phase as \"Completed\" if any subject within that phase becomes unchecked. This eliminates the need for a specific \"Rollback\" button, making the user experience smoother.\n\n\n**Adjusting Counter Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating logic to reactively adjust the \"Active Phase\" counter (`ciclo_atual`). When a phase transitions back to \"Active\" because a subject is unchecked, I'm ensuring the counter decreases accordingly. I am focusing on making the visualization of \"Completed,\" \"Active,\" and \"Locked\" phases dynamic. Specifically, I'm working to integrate the status mapping, which currently uses `isCompleted`, `isActive`, and `isLocked`, to incorporate the reactive adjustments to the counter, so the data model will be the source of truth, for visualization.\n\n\n**Automating Phase Selection**\n\nI'm now implementing the automatic calculation of `activeCicloId`. The active phase becomes the first phase containing incomplete subjects. When a subject toggles, `handleToggleMateria` will recalculate the active phase. I'm focusing on updating the `saveCycleState` function to handle `ciclo_atual` accurately with changes in `materias_concluidas_ids`. I'm working on how `activeCicloId` reacts to changes in completion status across different phases, ensuring it always points to the correct active phase.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
    "createdTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769384696,
      "nanos": 558000000
    },
    "doneTimestamp": {
      "seconds": 1769384708,
      "nanos": 92000000
    }
