    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Defining Component Changes**\n\nI'm focused on the `components/Ciclos.tsx` file for now, potentially dipping into `types.ts` only if absolutely necessary, aiming for minimal changes. My primary task involves adding a field for the number of cycles after the \"Daily Study (H)\" entry.\n\n\n**Refining Cycle Generation**\n\nI'm now honing the cycle generation behavior. Instead of auto-generating, there will be a \"Gerar Ciclo Sugerido\" button to initialize. This triggers a function updated to take the cycle number as a parameter, and then populates the active cycles. The UI's grid will change, and a new styling for the button will be applied.\n\n\n**Implementing Cycle Parameters**\n\nI'm updating the `services/cycleLogic.ts` file to accommodate the cycle number parameter. Specifically, I'm modifying the `gerarCiclos` function to accept `totalCycles`, which will be used in generating the cycles. Concurrently, the state variable `numCiclos` will be added, along with the UI elements for its input and the \"GERAR CICLO ESTRATÉGICO\" button in `components/Ciclos.tsx`. The auto-generation logic is removed, and now is a button action.\n\n\n**Analyzing Cycle Interactions**\n\nI'm now focusing on ensuring that cycle customizations aren't inadvertently overwritten when a new suggestion is generated. I'm taking the button-triggered generation as an \"AI/Algorithmic Suggestion\" concept, implying that the initial state might either be empty or reflect a previous customization, which should be protected from unintentional changes. I'll need to update `types.ts` to include `num_ciclos` in `StudyCycle`. I will also update `cycleLogic.ts` and `Ciclos.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Cycle Logic**\n\nI'm modifying the `gerarCiclos` function to accept `totalCycles` with a default of 4, replacing the hardcoded loop. My next step is to refine the \"Gerar Ciclo Sugerido\" button's visibility, making it appear only after subjects are configured. The input grid is now adjusted from `grid-cols-2` to `grid-cols-3` to accommodate the \"Qtde Ciclos\" input. I will need to update `types.ts`, `services/cycleLogic.ts`, and `components/Ciclos.tsx`.\n\n\n",
