      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Analyzing the Error Source**\n\nI'm currently focused on pinpointing the root cause of the \"num_ciclos\" column error within the \"Ciclos\" page. The system indicates a failure to locate this specific column in the `study_cycles` table. My priority is to understand why this column isn't being recognized by the schema cache. I will investigate schema definitions, model configurations, and database interactions.\n\n\n**Confirming Missing Column**\n\nThe analysis confirms the 'num_ciclos' column is absent from the Supabase table, according to the error message and confirmed by cross-referencing the schema. The error isn't stale schema cache as I initially suspected. It seems I will now need to review the payload data and any relevant configurations to determine where the column is intended to exist. I will prioritize checking configurations and code that interacts with the `study_cycles` table to understand where the system expects this column to be.\n\n\n**Investigating Payload Source**\n\nI've traced the missing column back to the `Ciclos.tsx` file. The provided code snippet reveals where the `num_ciclos` data is being constructed within the payload sent to the database. I am now examining how these updates are incorporated into the payload, checking for any inconsistencies or potential data type conflicts that might prevent the column from being properly recognized. I will need to look into how the payload variable interacts with the database.\n\n\n**Refining Column Inclusion**\n\nI've clarified the discrepancy: the payload includes several columns, such as `num_ciclos`, that are absent from the database schema. My focus is on rectifying this. I will first verify which columns exist in the DB, as the user's screenshot indicates `meta_atual` exists. Then, I'll store the additional configuration data in a JSONB column, likely `schedule`. I need to ensure the payload only includes columns present in the schema.\n\n\n**Consolidating Payload Data**\n\nI'm now consolidating the data to align with the database schema, focusing on the `schedule` column. I need to handle additional fields and verify existing columns, such as `meta_atual`. I am updating `schedule` to an object to include `materias_concluidas_ids` and other supplemental data. If this isn't sufficient, I may omit the missing columns from the top-level payload and rely on local state. I will omit `num_ciclos`, `ciclo_atual`, `metas_concluidas`, `materias_concluidas`.\n\n\n**Refactoring Payload Columns**\n\nI'm now refactoring the payload within `Ciclos.tsx` to streamline data handling and resolve the column error. My strategy centers on removing the non-existent columns from the direct payload and storing them either within the `schedule` JSONB field, or calculating them from the data contained within the `schedule`. I am simplifying the data structure by focusing on sending only the existing columns: `user_id`, `board`, `exam_date`, `hours_per_day`, `schedule`, and `meta_atual`. I plan to integrate the configuration data and cycle information into a more organized `schedule` object or array to keep data consistency, and to avoid unnecessary data transfer.\n\n\n**Adapting to Schema**\n\nI'm now implementing the revised strategy in `Ciclos.tsx`, focusing on aligning the payload with the database schema. I've removed the redundant fields, moving them into the `schedule` column, which I've confirmed as being present. I'm prioritizing the loading logic to ensure the application correctly reads from the new `schedule` object. I will then update the `StudyCycle` type definition to reflect the DB structure. This approach eliminates the column error by sending only compatible data.\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Payload**\n\nI'm now implementing changes in `Ciclos.tsx` to streamline the data structure for Supabase. My main focus is on organizing the data, so it's only using the allowed columns: `user_id`, `board`, `exam_date`, `hours_per_day`, `schedule`, and `meta_atual`. I am incorporating the cycles data, progress, and configuration within the `schedule` column. I have to make sure I update the `useEffect` hook to correctly read from the new structure.\n\n\n",
