    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Addressing Study Cycles**\n\nI'm currently focused on resolving the \"Ciclos\" page optimization. I've pinpointed several key issues: cycles generating without saving, a crash during save due to an ID type mismatch, and missing database columns. I'm prioritizing the save issue, given its critical impact.\n\n\n**Evaluating Database Structure**\n\nI'm now evaluating the database structure, specifically the `schedule` column's `jsonb` encapsulation. While the study cycle generation and save are working, I'm considering whether adding dedicated columns for `ciclo_atual`, `metas_concluidas`, `disciplinas_por_ciclo`, and `num_ciclos` would enhance query performance and reporting on the \"Ciclos\" page, given the user's feedback, and the successful resolution of the save issue.\n\n\n**Refining \"Ciclos\" UX**\n\nI'm now focused on refining the UX/UI of the \"Ciclos\" page. The current style is functional, but lacks polish. My plan is to make the \"Operational Matrix\" look more like the reference screenshot: darker, sharper, with better spacing. I also plan to add more interactive states, optimize the data structure (even with `jsonb`), and add a \"Smart Progress\" indicator that reflects the entire study plan's progress. Finally, I'll generate the SQL to add suggested columns for improved database performance.\n\n\n**Enhancing Page Aesthetics**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in making `Ciclos.tsx` \"World Class\". I'm going beyond just the existing `jsonb` fix. I plan to enhance the user interface with specific gradients and shadows, drawing inspiration from the \"Flow\" aesthetic in the image, to polish the visual experience. I'm focusing on key enhancements like phase auto-advance, smoother drag-and-drop interactions, and robust persistence against ID changes. I'll also provide a `database_fix.sql` file separately. I'll make sure to add the sidebar, too.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
    },
