omplete within `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm focused on how `isCicloComplete` is calculated, ensuring it correctly accounts for all required conditions and gracefully handles edge cases and data validation, especially around `m.instanceId` and comparing to `materiasConcluidasIds`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Cycle Logic**\n\nI'm now carefully examining how `nextActivePhaseId` is determined, focusing on the conditional logic within the loop that iterates through cycles and materials. I need to understand how the criteria for cycle completion are evaluated and if the assignment of `nextActivePhaseId` correctly reflects the intended cycle progression.\n\n\n**Reviewing Persistence Logic**\n\nI'm now diving into the `persistChanges` function and its integration with Supabase. I'm focusing on how new and existing cycles are handled and how the update/insert logic functions correctly. Specifically, I'm verifying the `cycleId` and the `payload` construction, as well as the error handling within the try-catch block to ensure reliable persistence of study cycle data. I am also checking state management.\n\n\n**Examining Materia Logic**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the `toggleMateria` function's logic and the data updates. I'm making sure `materiasConcluidasIds` correctly reflects the changes in the list of `materias` and that `persistChanges` is called at the correct time, ensuring it is properly persisting these updates and handling edge cases.\n\n\n**Verifying HUD Integration**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the HUD component's integration within the overall structure. I'm focusing on how the data, specifically `metaAtual`, is being passed to the HUD and if the presentation is aligned with the design, checking to see if `Target` and `Trophy` are coming from the same source as the other icons, and if the styling is consistent. I need to make sure this HUD will be properly displayed.\n\n\n**Evaluating HUD Integration**\n\nI'm now focusing on the integration of HUD, verifying how data like `metaAtual` flows through the component. I see there's a reference to icons `BrainCircuit` and `RefreshCw`, so I am verifying that these are correctly imported and being used in the HUD and that styles are consistent. The plan is to get the dashboard correctly rendered and functioning.\n\n\n**Evaluating Cycle Presentation**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the presentation of each cycle within `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm verifying the conditional styling using `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent` to make sure each cycle renders according to the correct logic, checking the `border` and `background` conditions, and that all data sources are used correctly. My goal is for this to be properly rendered.\n\n\n**Assessing Cycle Presentation**\n\nI'm now carefully checking how each study cycle displays in `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm confirming that the conditional styles correctly use `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent`, and that borders and backgrounds align with cycle states. I also want the presentation to render correctly based on these states.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Cycle Presentation**\n\nI'm now confirming the presentation of each cycle, including borders, backgrounds, and conditional styles using `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent` to ensure consistent and correct rendering based on state. I'm checking the data sources used to ensure all information aligns with the rendering.\n\n\n**Evaluating Cycle Display**\n\nI'm now methodically reviewing how each study cycle renders in `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm confirming that the conditional styling, which uses `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent`, correctly influences the visual appearance, focusing on borders and backgrounds.\n\n\n\n**Assessing Cycle Rendering**\n\nI'm now carefully checking how each study cycle displays in `Ciclos.tsx`. The conditional styling uses `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent` to correctly influence the visual appearance, focusing on borders and backgrounds. All of this ensures the correct state, and rendering properly.\n\n\n**Evaluating Cycle Display**\n\nI'm now methodically confirming the conditional styling in `Ciclos.tsx` using `isCurrent`, `isCompleted`, and `percent`. This styling correctly determines the visual appearance, focusing specifically on borders and backgrounds, and to ensure the correct state.\n\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Display**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the presentation of the configuration matrix within `Ciclos.tsx`, focusing on its styling and layout, like the padding and overall visual appearance. I'm verifying the alignment of the text elements and the use of the correct font sizes and weights.\n\n\n**Reviewing Component Styling**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the display, focusing on the configuration matrix's visual presentation. I'm carefully reviewing styling details like padding, alignment, and font choices to ensure visual consistency and readability. The layout and appearance should now look correct and functional.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Display**\n\nI'm now focusing on the configuration UI in `Ciclos.tsx`, specifically the styling for the \"Hrs Líquidas/Dia\" and \"Total Ciclos\" inputs. I am checking the classes, especially the text size, padding, and font styles, to ensure the input fields are aligned correctly.\n\n```\n<div className=\"space-y-2\">\n  <label className=\"text-[9px] font-black text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest ml-1\">Hrs Líquidas/Dia</label>\n  <input type=\"number\" value={hoursPerDay} onChange={e => setHoursPerDay(Math.max(1, parseInt(e.target.value)||1))} className=\"w-full bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 text-xs font-black text-white focus:border-indigo-500 outline-none transition-all\" />\n</div>\n<div className=\"space-y-2\">\n  <label className=\"text-[9px] font-black text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest ml-1\">Total Ciclos</label>\n  <input type=\"number\" value={numCiclos} onChange={e => setNumCiclos(Math.max(1, parseInt(e.target.value)||1))} className=\"w-full bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 text-xs font-black text-white focus:border-indigo-500 outline-none transition-all\" />\n</div>\n```\n\n\n**Refining Styling of Inputs**\n\nI'm now refining the styling of the input fields within the configuration matrix of `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm confirming text size, padding, and font styles are consistent, especially the `Hrs Líquidas/Dia` and `Total Ciclos` inputs. I also see that the classes are present, and the inputs should appear correct.\n\n\n**Evaluating Input Styling**\n\nI am now assessing the input field styling in the configuration area, particularly the dropdown and button within `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm confirming alignment, font sizes and weights, and overall visual harmony. The goal is to make sure these elements are consistent with the other styles on the page.\n\n\n**Evaluating Input Styling**\n\nI'm now carefully checking the `ANEXAR DISCIPLINA` button's styling within the cycle configuration. The goal is confirming alignment, sizes, font, and overall visual harmony with other page elements. I will also be verifying the styling and behavior of the \"GERAR NOVO PLANO DE CICLOS\" button.\n\n\n**Refining Subject Presentation**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the presentation of the subject list. I am verifying the alignment, sizing, and styling of elements within each subject entry, specifically focusing on the `Database` icon. I am ensuring that the visual elements are consistent and readable.\n\n\n**Refining Subject Presentation**\n\nI'm now refining how the subject list looks. I'm focusing on consistency in sizing, spacing, and styling of each entry, paying close attention to the `Database` icon. I will also make sure the alignment is correct to enhance readability.\n\n\n**Reviewing Delete Confirmation**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the delete confirmation dialog. I'm focusing on the dialog's design, typography, and button placement, and verifying the functionality and correct behavior of this dialog within