ycle);\n        addCycle(cycle);\n      });\n      addToast({\n        type: 'success',\n        title: 'Sucesso',\n        message: 'Ciclos gerados com sucesso!'\n      });\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(\"Erro ao gerar ciclos:\", error);\n      addToast({\n        type: 'error',\n        title: 'Erro',\n        message: 'Erro ao gerar os ciclos. Verifique as disciplinas configuradas.'\n      });\n    } finally {\n      setIsSaving(false);\n    }\n  };\n```\n\n\n**Verifying Generation Integration**\n\nI'm now carefully examining the integration of the `handleGenerate` function within `Ciclos.tsx`. I've made the addition and confirmed it interacts with `gerarCiclos` correctly, ensuring the correct data flow, including state updates. I also confirmed that it updates the loading state. I've re-examined the function to confirm all dependencies.\n\nI'm checking that this call gets the subjects from the local state:\n```tsx\n      const newCycles = await gerarCiclos(configSubjects, ciclosPorDia, totalCiclos, user.id);\n```\n\nI am verifying that this call saves the data:\n```tsx\n      newCycles.forEach(async (cycle) => {\n        await persistChanges(cycle);\n        addCycle(cycle);\n      });\n```\n\n\n**Finalizing Handle Generation**\n\nI've successfully integrated and verified the `handleGenerate` function, confirming its interaction with `gerarCiclos`, the local state, and the state updates. I have reviewed all changes for consistency. I have completed the final steps, implementing and verifying the solution.\n\n\n**Finalizing Cycle Updates**\n\nI'm now completing the review process. I have successfully created the function and confirmed all updates, including the state updates. The fix is now completely implemented. I'm checking the final call to the updated local function. I'm verifying data and checking for data consistency.\n\n\n**Finalizing Code Integration**\n\nI've completed integrating the handle generation and confirmed data consistency throug