red to deploy the updates.\n\n\n**Refining Time Display**\n\nI'm now focusing on optimizing the time display within the cycle list, particularly the format used for hours and minutes. I am considering refining the calculations to handle the values more efficiently, and now I'm checking the calculations and its interactions.\n\n\n**Refining Logic Integration**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating `handleArchiveAndAdvance`, ensuring it correctly updates state related to cycle advancement. I'm verifying the incrementing of `metaAtual` and `metasConcluidas`, and the correct reset of `materiasConcluidasIds`, along with persistence using `persistChanges`, as indicated. I've re-examined the code, confirming that it's working as expected.\n\n\n**Refining Component Display**\n\nI'm now implementing the refactored code block, specifically focusing on the component display aspects to ensure visual consistency and responsiveness, also paying attention to ensuring all the logic has been implemented. I'm verifying the states associated with each item are working.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Element**\n\nI'm now carefully implementing the display refinements. I've focused on ensuring the visual elements for cycle subjects display correctly, including state-based styling for completion and swap actions. I've re-examined the code, confirming that it's working as expected, and I'm ready to continue.\n\n\n**Refining Button Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the integration and styling of the archive button and the associated logic, especially regarding the 'disabled' state when the percentage is less than 100 or when isSaving is true. I am verifying the `handleArchiveAndAdvance` functionality and any state updates. I also verified the visual styling.\n\n\n**Refining Display Logic**\n\nI'm now implementing the display logic. I'm focusing on ensuring UI updates reflect state changes. I am checking elements for data, especially relating to completion and advancement. I've examined UI elements to verify data consistency and responsiveness. I'm continuing the implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Code Review**\n\nI'm now closely analyzing all the implemented code, confirming the accurate integration of all components and the intended data flow. I'm verifying all aspects of functionality, including UI states, ensuring seamless integration and data consistency throughout.\n\n\n**Refining Code Integration**\n\nI'm now integrating the functions and verifying correct component behavior, focusing on UI consistency and data integrity. I am confirming states.\n\n\n**Confirming Final Implementation**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided code block to incorporate the subject configuration UI into the component, making the selection persistent. I have focused on the implementation to handle the local state updates. I confirm the proper data alignment and state synchronization.\n\nI'm examining the `select` elements and ensuring their behavior is consistent and working correctly.\n\n\n**Finalizing Component Integration**\n\nI've completed the integration of the code block for the subject configuration UI. I've focused on ensuring the selection and updates for configuration are working and persistent in the data. I'm verifying the functionality of the UI elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Subject Configuration**\n\nI'm now integrating the provided subject configuration UI into `Ciclos.tsx`. I'm focusing on ensuring persistent selection and local state updates. I'm verifying the functionality of the provided UI elements, specifically the `select` element.\n\n\n",
