      "text": "**Clarifying The Scope**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the project's true scope. While the initial prompt focuses on the site name, there are clues suggesting a broader task, including replacing \"FLOW\" with \"KRONOS\". It seems I should also be considering the use of a favicon, according to a reference. I am now reconciling the initial, limited prompt with these hints.\n\n\n**Defining The Specifics**\n\nI've got a clearer picture of the required changes. My focus is now on the precise tasks: renaming the site, updating the icon, and ensuring consistent branding. I'm looking to update `App.tsx`, `index.html`, `Login.tsx`, and potentially `Ciclos.tsx`. In `index.html`, I will update the `<title>`. In `App.tsx`, I'll change the sidebar text and the `BrainCircuit` icon (possibly with a custom SVG or Lucide). All references to \"StudyFlow\" must also be updated.\n\n\n**Refining The Implementation**\n\nI'm now diving into the code changes. Specifically, in `Login.tsx`, I'll update the title to \"KRONOS\" and swap the icon to my custom stopwatch SVG. The `metadata.json` file requires the name change to \"KRONOS Pro AI\". I'm also planning CSS gradients to match the neon stopwatch image. I'll define my custom `<KronosIcon />` and ensure consistency across `index.html`, `App.tsx`, and `Login.tsx`. I have the title as \"KRONOS - Master UI\" and the name in metadata.json is now set.\n\n\n",
