    "author": "model",
    "payload": {
      "type": "thinking",
      "text": "**Designing the Header Clock**\n\nOkay, I'm focusing on the `App.tsx` header. My aim is to add a digital clock next to the existing date display, mimicking an airport clock design. The challenge now is deciding on the specific digital display style – should it be flip-style or segmented? I also need to make sure this new clock looks nice next to the current site name!\n\n\n**Refining the Neon Vibe**\n\nI'm now integrating the neon stopwatch aesthetic and \"KRONOS\" branding from the provided image. I've been experimenting with `App.tsx` and trying to align the new clock with the existing \"Airport/Master UI\" style. I'm focusing on the `<header>` element and ensuring that the digital clock design blends well with the current site title display. I'm aiming for a cohesive look.\n\n\n**Implementing the Digital Clock**\n\nI'm now implementing the digital, segmented clock, focusing on neon colors to fit the KRONOS branding. I've decided on an \"Inter black\" font for a modern look. The goal is to make it appear next to the calendar in the right side of the header. I'm prioritizing high contrast text, and a glowing container style. I'm thinking bg-black/80, border-white/5, and shadow-inner. The time will update every second.\n\n\n**Positioning the Digital Clock**\n\nOkay, I'm now focusing on integrating the digital clock next to the existing date display. I've got the clock ticking and displaying the time in a neon cyan format. I'm leveraging the `useState` hook for the time and `setInterval` to keep it updated. Right now, I'm concentrating on the positioning of the clock within the `App.tsx` header to align it next to the date.\n\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
